<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c48a9b9e-b666-4c79-8a44-08a23d094316> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Lazy/deferred text export (mark-dirty, write on shutdown or on demand) instead of synchronous write-through — rejected: a user can capture then immediately git commit, and shutdown is unreliable (SIGKILL); at ~2k quads the synchronous export costs milliseconds, and always-in-sync store/text makes the startup three-way compare unambiguous." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5e08352-ff6e-484c-bb48-1a22efc3a009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Alternative> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5e08352-ff6e-484c-bb48-1a22efc3a009> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A staging named graph for proposed edges (move edge between project and proposals graphs on accept/reject) — rejected: the canonical kg.nq export is project-graph-only (src/export.rs; ExportScope has no third scope) and graph_import::validate_import_graphs BAILS on any non-project/provenance graph, so a proposals graph would be primary data stranded in the gitignored RocksDB cache, violating Req d459cac2 (committed text is the source of truth). Making it round-trip would mean invasively extending the most safety-critical persistence code for a transient feature." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5e08352-ff6e-484c-bb48-1a22efc3a009> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5e08352-ff6e-484c-bb48-1a22efc3a009> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5e08352-ff6e-484c-bb48-1a22efc3a009> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-13T05:30:43.715521Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5e08352-ff6e-484c-bb48-1a22efc3a009> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A staging named graph for proposed edges (move edge between project and proposals graphs on accept/reject) — rejected: the canonical kg.nq export is project-graph-only (src/export.rs; ExportScope has no third scope) and graph_import::validate_import_graphs BAILS on any non-project/provenance graph, so a proposals graph would be primary data stranded in the gitignored RocksDB cache, violating Req d459cac2 (committed text is the source of truth). Making it round-trip would mean invasively extending the most safety-critical persistence code for a transient feature." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5fd1925-a8a9-4000-93e5-0cd0b02924d5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Alternative> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
