<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/007dce15-98de-4494-8c64-1729d9e93d66> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/007dce15-98de-4494-8c64-1729d9e93d66> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Automatic capture is a telemetry journal, not a record minter" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/007dce15-98de-4494-8c64-1729d9e93d66> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/783a4b9e-8649-4154-a158-751bd1058e05> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/007dce15-98de-4494-8c64-1729d9e93d66> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/007dce15-98de-4494-8c64-1729d9e93d66> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Automatic (adapter-initiated) captures — the Claude Code Stop hook and the opencode session push — never write to the knowledge graph. POST /api/v1/capture appends a fire-log journal entry (host, summary, changed files) and mints nothing; no proposed record, no inbox entry. Deliberate capture remains the only minting path: record_important_decision and an agent explicitly invoking the MCP capture_decision_point tool. Evidence for the demotion: across the entire life of automatic capture (v2.2, 2026-07-13 → 2026-07-15) not one auto-minted record was ratified — every specimen was a status message (\"Blocked: …\", \"Waiting on the test suite…\", \"What would you like to clarify…\") because a session's final message is a report to the user, not a decision, and no symbolic guard can distinguish the two by timing alone. The maintainer's verdict: these are prompt/build statuses that do not belong in the graph at all. The trial arms never depended on auto-minting (their daemons predate v2.2), so nothing loses record accumulation. The fires journal keeps the auditable session breadcrumb (invariant #6) without polluting the graph; the [trial-fire] kill-metric tally reads labeled graph records, not the fires log, so telemetry entries cannot inflate it." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/007dce15-98de-4494-8c64-1729d9e93d66> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
