<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0765610c-e0cf-4fbc-a370-08dd3c019ddb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0765610c-e0cf-4fbc-a370-08dd3c019ddb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Session-pinned substrate with refresh-before-dispatch" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0765610c-e0cf-4fbc-a370-08dd3c019ddb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0765610c-e0cf-4fbc-a370-08dd3c019ddb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0765610c-e0cf-4fbc-a370-08dd3c019ddb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code-recovery" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/0765610c-e0cf-4fbc-a370-08dd3c019ddb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: each Knowledge-LSP session serves every position-bearing surface from a session-pinned Arc<Substrate> snapshot that advances ONLY in refresh_if_state_changed - together with every open document's base_text and a republish - and refresh runs before dispatching EVERY message, not just on the 2s idle tick. This closes the codex-review P1: AppState::substrate() reloads lazily from any caller, so a request could previously map old-baseline document positions against a newer index, and continuous traffic postponed repair indefinitely. All five direct substrate call sites in the session (file_diagnostics, code_lenses, code_actions, propose_link_command, refresh itself) use the pin; hover - which reached the substrate indirectly through get_entity_dossier's Position target - now resolves the position against the pinned substrate and fetches the dossier by Symbol, whose identity is generation-independent (get_entity_dossier's signature is unchanged for MCP/policy; its cosmetic churn/stale-banner substrate reads stay live). Same review's companion fixes, landed together: (1) didChange republishes push diagnostics (the buffer's line alignment is renderable state - push-surface rule, Lesson 6691839b), with a per-file memo of the git-log commit instant so typing does not spawn a subprocess per keystroke (cleared on open/save and on generation change); (2) git hooks use `moosedev index --if-idle` (try-lock skip on this repository's index.lock) instead of a global pgrep that false-positived across repositories; the daemon's debounced runner still WAITS - a scheduled run represents needed reconciliation and is never skipped; (3) scheduler shutdown uses a commit-then-recheck protocol (worker stores `running` then re-checks `stop` before invoking the runner) so a shutdown racing an imminent run provably never joins through a ~49s producer run; (4) AppState reload failures memoize exactly the sampled manifest via Substrate::load_with (the previous path re-read the manifest inside load, so a failure on a mid-load-appearing generation memoized the wrong identity and retried forever); (5) generation publish fsyncs the parent generations/ directory so a crash cannot keep meta.json while losing the directory entry it references. Verified: 21 lsp_diagnostics tests (incl. new didChange line-shift republish), 7 scheduler unit tests (incl. a 20-iteration shutdown-race latency loop), 13 producer tests (incl. try-lock and if-idle-skip), hover/transport/reload suites, clippy -D warnings clean, live two-cycle didSave check re-passed on the rebuilt daemon, and a live --if-idle skip against an in-flight run." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
