<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Instrument per-query NLQ token usage" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/f4d2f589-8f00-4640-ae16-fbb0184cb365> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Phase 1 of the value benchmark. MOOSE's LlmClient trait returns only the completion string, so OpenAiCompatClient (src/llm/mod.rs) now accumulates usage.prompt_tokens/completion_tokens via interior mutability (Arc<UsageCounters> of two AtomicU64), populated in chat_completion from the response body. Added with_fresh_usage() (a clone sharing the HTTP pool but with FRESH counters) and take_usage() (read + reset). graph::query() forks the client per call so token counts attribute to exactly one query even under concurrent shared-backend use, then appends a machine-parseable 'tokens: prompt=X completion=Y' line to the rendered trace. This lets the benchmark attribute B2's INTERNAL NLQ cost (which B1's embedding retrieval does not incur) for an honest total-cost comparison. No MOOSE change needed: the NLQ LLM calls route back through our chat_completion sensor (execute_graph_walk_nlq_with_context is passed &state.llm), so this stays within the open boundary (invariants #8, #11). Verified: 3 new unit tests (accumulate/reset, missing-fields→0, fork isolation), cargo clippy --all-targets clean, full cargo test suite green." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T15:19:32.540109Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/1f749613-6ec4-481f-8a43-2d1c050d89b8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Instrument per-query NLQ token usage in the LLM client; surface in the query trace" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "openEntity lens command is server-handled via window/showDocument" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/f79f0b2f-fdc1-4261-9f6b-d4c2455aace0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the code-lens command `moosedev.openEntity` is executed by the server (added to executeCommandProvider; handled in the LSP session), which resolves the entity's workbench URL and sends a fire-and-forget `window/showDocument` request with external:true — so lenses are clickable in every editor with zero per-client glue. Why: all four target clients (VS Code, Neovim 0.10+, eglot, lsp-mode) support showDocument, while client-side command registration differs per editor and is impossible in eglot (no client command registry). Compatible with AD fb61ce61's no-response-plumbing session: the run loop still drops client responses, and showDocument's reply is ignorable, so the new outbound-request path (session-local id counter, `send_server_request`) is fire-and-forget only. Degradations are deliberate product tone: lens on an unminted entity (no arguments) → info message, workbench not serving (no http.addr file) → info message, client without showDocument → info message carrying the URL; a malformed or unminted entity IRI is InvalidParams (the minted-entity check doubles as URL hygiene since the uuid segment lands in a browser). Zero UI/API changes needed: the workbench `#/record/<uuid>` route already resolves any typed project-graph subject, CodeEntities included (workbench_entity_url delegates to workbench_record_url). Proven by tests/lsp_open_entity.rs (showDocument round-trip ordering, fallbacks, InvalidParams) and the Neovim conformance round-trip (headless handler answers {success:true} and asserts the /#/record/ URL)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T04:38:55.501499Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "openEntity lens command is server-handled via window/showDocument" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/13943a5f-0bc3-47f5-99b4-afb42d22ac09> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20145567-549e-4b33-be43-32e7f0f20a1a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/46ac8f88-afc0-4287-8422-bbc961b27726> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ratification queue: reified code:ProposedLink in the project graph, not a staging graph" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/27f9d9b8-3df9-44bf-9d2a-bd2270212de1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "James" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a proposed record→code-entity link (from the citation-seed migration, and future capture) is represented as a code:ProposedLink node in the PROJECT graph carrying the proposed triple — subject record IRI, predicate local name, target substrate symbol + path — as LITERALS plus arch:hasLifecycleStatus (proposed→accepted/rejected), never the real link edge. So a pending proposal is invisible to dossiers and the why-coverage metric (which walk only the five real link predicates concerns/constrains/satisfies/embodies/violates) until ratified. accept_proposal materializes the real edge via link_code (re-resolving the symbol at HEAD) then flips status→accepted; reject_proposal flips→rejected and never creates an edge; both preserve the node + evidence as audit (invariant #6). Honesty holds BY CONSTRUCTION: ProposedLink asserts none of the link predicates, is not an InformationRecord subclass (excluded from every record listing and require_information_record), is declared in the code vocab (out of the ABox vector index), and GROWL drops the rdf:type completion so it never gains rdf:type InformationRecord from the reused arch predicates (a regression test locks this). Ontology delta: one class + four datatype props (proposesSubject/Predicate/TargetSymbol/TargetPath) in software-code.ttl, NO SHACL shape (parked-discipline — the literals are written directly, never oriented through relate(), so no relation-catalogue write path). Rejected alternative below. Implemented v2.1: src/graph/proposals.rs." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-13T05:30:43.715521Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Ratification queue: reified code:ProposedLink in the project graph, not a staging graph" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/20a15361-19e9-43fb-920c-a215eefc531f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/c5e08352-ff6e-484c-bb48-1a22efc3a009> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/228b272c-bd92-489c-9734-dcb95b060de2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/228b272c-bd92-489c-9734-dcb95b060de2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "v2 code ontology: separate software/code# module generated via Trivyn, brief as input-of-record" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/228b272c-bd92-489c-9734-dcb95b060de2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/228b272c-bd92-489c-9734-dcb95b060de2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the v2 code-layer ontology terms (the 8 alignment-cleared classes: CodeEntity, CodeSnapshot, CodeFile, CodeRole, Criticality, AttentionPolicy, Observation, AuthorshipProvenance) are minted as a SEPARATE module generated by Trivyn's ontology pipeline — hash-style namespace https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/code# with shapes at …/software/code/shapes# (per AD f68ef43e) — which IMPORTS and specializes the software-engineering module under its Component/Module lineage, rather than growing the shipped software-engineering TTL in place. This occupies the extension seam the v1 architecture-ontology brief reserved ('language-specific (deferred) — specializes SE'), generalized to language-AGNOSTIC: language specifics live in the SCIP substrate identity scheme, never in the ontology. The generation input-of-record is spec/code-ontology-brief.md (structure mirrors spec/architecture-ontology-brief.md): it fixes layering, the 8 classes by stratum, seed relations (playsRole/hasCriticality carrying status+provenance, declaredIn crossing the two containment hierarchies, refactor-continuity edges, hasSnapshot/observedIn, intent links realizes/satisfies/embodies, constrains/violates widened), per-stratum SHACL posture, and the paste-ready domain-hint prompt (§9) for the generator; it defers to the generator the BFO grounding of CodeEntity vs CodeSnapshot, reification vs RDF-star for status-carrying assertions, and kind/exposure as designators vs shallow subclasses. Encodes, does not re-litigate: ADs b0d3e4d9 (three strata), b5b4762b (role taxonomy, ratified 2026-07-06), 136dbf24 (entity identity), 7079634f (intent links), and the 2026-07-03 alignment pass (reuse Interface/InterfaceDefinition/Module/DataStore/Constraint and dependsOn/implements/uses/accesses/exposes; never re-mint)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/228b272c-bd92-489c-9734-dcb95b060de2> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
