<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/30ec7728-73db-4483-a5e3-e2778fdd16df> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/afe48c12-3968-40a1-9690-8dba8087155f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31a1a44a-ce7c-4d3f-87bb-ea30ede8c940> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31a1a44a-ce7c-4d3f-87bb-ea30ede8c940> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Web UI binds ephemeral loopback port; http.addr invalidated on startup" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31a1a44a-ce7c-4d3f-87bb-ea30ede8c940> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31a1a44a-ce7c-4d3f-87bb-ea30ede8c940> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Refines the web-UI binding sub-decision of AD d8a5cff1 (fixed 127.0.0.1:7474 → MOOSEDEV_HTTP_ADDR defaulting to 127.0.0.1:0): the OS assigns a free ephemeral loopback port, avoiding collisions across per-data-dir backends. The backend publishes the resolved address to <data_dir>/http.addr for cross-process discovery (--status, ui, generated hooks), and — the correction over the superseded claim — spawn_http_if_enabled now INVALIDATES any existing http.addr before every startup path (invalidate_http_addr, unit-tested), rewriting it only on a successful bind. The file's presence therefore always describes the CURRENT run: a crash followed by an HTTP-disabled or bind-failed restart leaves no stale address for cross-process readers to trust, closing the reclaimed-port hazard for hook policy payloads. In-process consumers (workbench-URL rendering) never read the file at all — they use the AppState-published bound address (AD a97f14e9). Unchanged from the superseded decision: spawn_http_if_enabled stays infallible (bind failure logs and returns None; the MCP backend keeps running), --status reports liveness via a socket connect that never opens RocksDB (Lesson c33ec85f), moosedev ui / --serve --open open the browser via a dependency-free launcher, and the conservative localhost-only default stands (Lesson 237dd9e8; MOOSEDEV_HTTP_ADDR for a stable port or network exposure, MOOSEDEV_NO_HTTP=1 to disable)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/31a1a44a-ce7c-4d3f-87bb-ea30ede8c940> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
