<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/346bb120-6855-421e-bb6b-1d778cfeb038> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Optional LLM assistance; symbolic default without provider" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/346bb120-6855-421e-bb6b-1d778cfeb038> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/346bb120-6855-421e-bb6b-1d778cfeb038> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "MOOSEDev's core memory server must be fully usable without an LLM provider; absent MOOSEDEV_LLM_BASE_URL pins assist level to PureSymbolic. The LLM remains an optional sensor for assisted NLQ/chat, not a runtime prerequisite for capture, get_relevant_context, sparql, validation, or symbolic query. Implementation: LlmConfig treats MOOSEDEV_LLM_BASE_URL as the opt-in flag, AppState records llm_configured and clamps the engine assist level to PureSymbolic when false, /health reports the effective LLM mode, and /chat returns 503 with an enablement message when no provider is configured. Verified with cargo check plus focused llm/query/API tests." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/346bb120-6855-421e-bb6b-1d778cfeb038> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/346bb120-6855-421e-bb6b-1d778cfeb038> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T20:16:48.444158Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/346bb120-6855-421e-bb6b-1d778cfeb038> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Optional LLM assistance; symbolic default without provider" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/346bb120-6855-421e-bb6b-1d778cfeb038> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/350c7f2e-61bd-49e4-b7cd-2fdd3f51f521> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Check distractors are drawn from the Story's own evidence and ranked symbolically" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/8d48edbd-7ee2-4a52-9eac-f2a09c858637> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/f4d2f589-8f00-4640-ae16-fbb0184cb365> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a comprehension check's wrong answers are selected from evidence the Story ACTUALLY SHOWED, ranked by a deterministic symbolic tier order, and never by the incidental ordering of whatever container held the candidates.\n\nTHE FAILURE. `unambiguous_check_options` iterated a `BTreeMap` keyed on the normalized option LABEL and took the first non-matching entries, so distractors were \"whatever sorts first\". TypeScript object-literal keys minted as CodeEntities (`'& h1'0`, `'background-color'0`) begin with an apostrophe and therefore sort before every real identifier — the quiz deterministically selected the worst candidates in the graph. A live Story for \"NLQ & retrieval pipeline\" asked which code entity realizes it and offered `'& h1'0` and `'& code'0`.\n\nThe pool was wrong too. Distractors came from a global sweep (a 96-record `relevant_context_snapshot`, or every component's records) rather than from the run's own evidence, so questions were answerable by topic word-overlap against titles the reader had never seen — testing vocabulary, not understanding.\n\nTHE RANKING, highest tier first, with a deterministic hash of the IRI as tie-break: (1) evidence displayed in THIS Story but not matching the target — the reader just read it, so answering requires having understood which subject it belonged to; (2) same kind as the correct answer, so the answer's kind cannot leak it; (3) a neighbouring component, by shared `covers_paths` prefix; (4) anything else eligible. Code-entity options additionally reject non-identifier labels.\n\nSELECTION STAYS DETERMINISTIC; only PRESENTATION is randomized. Constraint c1b8a8db makes deterministic checks authoritative, and Lesson bd79c33c requires independently ordered options and opaque per-option tokens — `opaque_options` already provides both and is untouched.\n\nHONEST DEGRADATION IS PRESERVED: when no plausible distractor exists the check is omitted and the missing assessment is a gap, never a trivial question.\n\nREJECTED — generating distractors with the LLM. It would produce plausible options immediately, and it was the first instinct on seeing the bad quiz. It breaks the authority split the Story rests on: Constraint c1b8a8db makes symbolic checks authoritative and LLM prose a non-authoritative presentation sensor, and the UI's promise to the reader is that answers are \"checked against graph relationships, not generated prose\". An invented wrong answer is ungrounded content in the one place the product claims grounding. It would also have hidden a plain ordering bug behind a model. LLM assistance may still earn a role in PHRASING a question or ranking already-eligible candidates; it must never choose or grade the answer." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/34e64e06-df7b-4f93-ada5-ee053abbb79a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T20:35:27.328343Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
