<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The fires.jsonl append-only telemetry log (spec §4.4) is deferred from the v2.0 slice list to v2.2, where the events it records actually exist: push-fires and gate-fires are active-agency verbs, and v2.0 ships only read surfaces (hover, diagnostics). A writer with no writers would be dead scaffolding. When v2.2's policy engine lands, the log lands with its first caller. Decided by James 2026-07-09 during slice-3 planning; this record is the conscious amendment of the spec's letter." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-09T23:54:58.831873Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Fire-event telemetry deferred to v2.2 (spec §4.4 amendment)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/6505ed72-0353-4b5b-9cc9-4039538f89e8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/365adb90-86c1-4478-b06f-129ab628a407> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/5596d4f4-bbd6-42bd-8263-1b18e83de944> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3a2de2e1-87d2-4bc7-85d2-ee103c5cf1bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3a2de2e1-87d2-4bc7-85d2-ee103c5cf1bc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recall replies are budget-bounded, truncating rather than dropping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3a2de2e1-87d2-4bc7-85d2-ee103c5cf1bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/3a2de2e1-87d2-4bc7-85d2-ee103c5cf1bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: `get_relevant_context` renders within a character budget shared across the returned records, shortening by TRUNCATION in preference to omission, and stating what it shortened.\n\nTHE FAILURE. Server instructions tell agents to call `get_relevant_context` with no `topic` for a broad inventory and `limit` up to 100. Rendering every record whole made exactly that call exceed the MCP response limit: measured on the dogfood graph at v0.7.0, limit=50 produced 90,712 chars and limit=100 produced 123,699 — the agent got an error instead of its memory, on the call CLAUDE.md prescribes as recall-first. Two bloat sources: full `hasDescription` bodies (3,000+ chars each), and repeated relation predicates on hub records — one SystemComponent carries ~70 bare `isConcernedBy` IRIs, costly and uninformative without labels.\n\nTHE SHAPE. Every byte a record emits — header, properties, IRI — is charged against its share of the budget (the even split, or a floor at large `limit`). Two independent caps: per-predicate, so one repeated relation cannot crowd out the description on a record whose links are enumerated first; and per-record, so no record consumes the reply.\n\nTRUNCATION MUST BE REACHABLE. Rendering reserves the framing — the key, the newline, and the exact truncation marker — BEFORE clipping, so a shortened line fits the room it was granted. Clipping to the full room and appending the marker afterwards (the first implementation) pushed every truncated line back over budget, so it was dropped and the value disappeared. A value is omitted only when even a floor-length lead will not fit. Budgets are byte counts while a `String` may only be split on a char boundary, so clipping walks back to the nearest one.\n\nBOUNDING THE UNBOUNDED. `rdfs:label` is clipped like any other value. Charging an arbitrarily long label to a record's share without clipping it left the reply unbounded for imported data no matter what the properties did — a ceiling that held only for well-behaved records is not a ceiling.\n\nHONESTY. Shortening is never silent: the reply states how many values were truncated and how many were not shown, and names the ways to the full text (narrow `topic`, lower `limit`, or `sparql`). Each record's IRI is always emitted whole, because it is how the caller reads back what was left out. This makes the shallow-browse rung of the get_relevant_context → query → sparql ladder (AD ee900bdb) explicit in its own output.\n\nMEASURED, same graph: limit=10 → 7,173 chars, limit=50 → 28,989, limit=100 → 26,319. Sharpens Lesson aec883f5 (the 100 cap; use sparql for complete reads): the cap was never the only reason a list-all is not a complete read — now the reply says so itself." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
