<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Syntactic fallback entities: lazy-mint-only, liveness-gated synthesis, positive-evidence orphaning" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/94e9028d-7a46-4c24-9a3a-f579d0e14537> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/aac4a555-e09f-4adf-8cb5-3134e864c0d4> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "phase7-acceptance" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Refines AD 992f3f10 (dual substrate: SCIP canonical, tree-sitter honest-degradation fallback) at the graph boundary. ts: identities are self-describing (ts:rust:<path>:<kind>:<qualified-name>; parsing is splitn(5) because qualified names contain ::). definition_for_symbol synthesizes a DefinitionEntry directly from the identity, but only when the declaration is verified alive on disk (identity_alive == Some(true)) — so link_code by symbol can never mint a guess; a dead or unverifiable identity is an error, not a write. Fallback entries always carry is_public = false, so the batch mint never sees them (lazy-mint-only via link_code). The mint orphan report marks a ts: entity orphaned only on positive evidence — the file or the exact declaration is provably gone; unverifiable (no substrate, no repo root) is never orphaned. Substrate::can_anchor extends the honest not-indexed replies: an uncovered file with a supported grammar on disk is anchorable, so it gets the plain reply rather than the not-indexed one." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/48f5d625-0541-49dc-824f-4b42a18cc7bc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-11T00:12:49.578573Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
