<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/b0bbcd2c-29aa-435c-9f8a-52ebd3081250> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/10f87e0d-a027-4331-909b-b6e3b20eaa0f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/45df40ee-4780-4ceb-b0f6-9ee177954185> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4aa634b8-60a2-4efc-af40-e3ce74cbb97c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/fd0dd350-6bdd-4f5f-8d73-b5f8cf88c59d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4bbb2125-2e2d-4a3f-9ab2-0b3ed55a1864> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4bbb2125-2e2d-4a3f-9ab2-0b3ed55a1864> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Split the benchmark baseline into B1-md and B1-rag" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4bbb2125-2e2d-4a3f-9ab2-0b3ed55a1864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4bbb2125-2e2d-4a3f-9ab2-0b3ed55a1864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Refines the arm design of benchmark AD 47f3f038. Prompted by the observation that modern AGENTIC coding tools mostly do NOT use embedding/vector retrieval over code: Claude Code, opencode (our driver), and Aider use agentic search (grep/glob/read) + structural maps (LSP, tree-sitter repo maps); embeddings persist mainly in IDE tools (Cursor @codebase, Continue/Windsurf), and Sourcegraph Cody dropped embeddings. Our B0 confirmed this — it grepped/read, no vector index. Implication: a single 'free-text RAG' B1 is not the most realistic competitor. Two things get retrieved — the CODE (agents grep it) and the captured RATIONALE/why (what MOOSEDev structures). So the free-text baseline is split into TWO arms, both content-parity with B2 (same captured records, different representation): (1) B1-md = the same rationale written as MARKDOWN DOCS in the working tree, consumed by the agent's NATIVE grep/read — the realistic 'team just kept decisions in docs/ADRs' competitor and how agents actually consume docs; (2) B1-rag = a recall() MCP tool over the rationale (BM25 now, optionally embeddings) — maps to the README's literal 'free text + embeddings' memory-tool claim. Headline comparisons become B2 − B1-md (realistic) and B2 − B1-rag (stated claim). This REVISES the earlier 'B1 must be a competent embedding RAG / upgrade BM25 to embeddings' guardrail: embeddings are not the fair/realistic default for a coding agent; markdown-in-tree + agentic search is. Arm ladder: B0 (code only) → B1-md (code + rationale markdown, grep) → B1-rag (code + recall tool) → B2 (code + MOOSEDev graph). User-confirmed 'both'." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4bbb2125-2e2d-4a3f-9ab2-0b3ed55a1864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4bbb2125-2e2d-4a3f-9ab2-0b3ed55a1864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T16:28:45.875304Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4bbb2125-2e2d-4a3f-9ab2-0b3ed55a1864> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Split the benchmark free-text baseline into B1-md (markdown-in-tree, agentic search) + B1-rag (recall tool); reflects how agentic coding tools actually retrieve" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Diagnostics push suppressed for pull-capable clients" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/4975ef04-fdb5-4272-9a66-b11cad326066> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the LSP session records the client's textDocument.diagnostic capability at initialize and suppresses the unconditional publishDiagnostics pushes (didOpen/didChange/didSave and the generation-refresh republish loop) for clients that advertise pull. Why: the server previously pushed AND advertised diagnosticProvider; Neovim 0.10+ auto-enables pull when the capability is advertised and renders push and pull in SEPARATE namespaces, so every squiggle double-reported — a real shipped bug, caught by the July 2026 editor-client capability research. Mechanics: publish_current_diagnostics early-returns when pull_diagnostics; on a substrate/graph generation change, pull clients get one fire-and-forget workspace/diagnostic/refresh request instead of a republish — only when workspace.diagnostic.refreshSupport is advertised and never for the initial generation pin (a refresh at session start is noise); clients without refreshSupport re-pull on their own triggers. The push path is retained verbatim for pull-less clients (eglot < 1.20, Neovim 0.9). Shutdown retraction stays unconditional: an empty publish is a harmless no-op in a namespace a pull client never populated, and refresh is never sent at shutdown (it would trigger re-pulls against a dying server). Proven by deterministic ordering tests in tests/lsp_diagnostics.rs (single-threaded writer: response-before-any-publish, refresh-on-generation-change, quiet-at-session-start) and the Neovim conformance publish counter (must be 0)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-19T04:44:26.202344Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Diagnostics push suppressed for pull-capable clients" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/4a4a0282-01f9-44da-9989-0034a16160c1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/27bee11c-ee86-4b48-bb40-05f0405f912d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4c1fe45d-2114-4245-95a0-f15e47853485> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/a09bff8f-b392-4562-88a7-43aa93964e19> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mint-gap visibility is the LAST dossier rung, below substrate coverage" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: 0.7.1 answers Requirement a0581252 with VISIBILITY only — three surfaces say when a store has an indexed substrate and no CodeEntity records — and on the dossier that message is the LAST rung, reached only after every substrate check has passed.\n\nORDERING (the correction). `get_entity_dossier`'s degradation ladder runs: (1) no substrate → run `index`; (2) position not anchorable → the per-producer coverage report; (3) store holds zero CodeEntities → run `mint`; (4) otherwise the plain no-recorded-knowledge reply. Rung 3 must come last because it is the only one that presumes a working index: a never-indexed project and a file outside the substrate both satisfy \"zero CodeEntities\" while `mint` would do nothing for either. Checking it first — as the superseded record specified — turned honest, actionable diagnostics into misdirection. The rung is still selector-independent (position, symbol, and IRI all reach it), which was the sound half of the original reasoning; only its position in the ladder was wrong.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED. A `has_any_code_entities` existence probe (deliberately NOT `entities_by_symbol`, which materializes every entity into a BTreeMap and already sits on the per-hover path), wired to: (1) a daemon startup warning naming the definition count and the fix; (2) the dossier rung above; (3) an LSP hover setup notice. All three share one message constant so they cannot drift.\n\nSILENCE-RULE SCOPE. The hover notice fires ONLY when the store has zero CodeEntities store-wide. Surfacing it per unminted symbol would put a popup on every identifier and break AD 8f20452a; the store-wide case is a configuration error, not knowledge.\n\nVERIFIED by reconstructing the trial-store condition (moose-trial's real 64,101-definition substrate against an empty graph): startup warned, all three selectors returned the diagnostic, then `mint --apply` created 5,066 entities and every surface went quiet. Regression-locked by tests/mcp_replies.rs: `unminted_store_reports_mint_without_masking_coverage` asserts the rung fires for position and symbol yet never displaces the coverage report, and `dossier_and_link_code_distinguish_substrate_coverage` now mints its fixture so it still exercises coverage rather than this rung.\n\nWHY NOT AUTOMATE. The daemon owns the RocksDB write lock and the reindex scheduler, so an in-process mint is a contained reuse of `mint_mode`'s body — the objection is not difficulty. It is that auto-mint makes MOOSEDev write CodeEntities and rewrite the committed kg.nq with no human action; at 5,066 entities for moose, doing that on every didSave-debounced generation is constant churn in a version-controlled artifact. Requirement a0581252 stays open." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/dbae9fe2-a423-4cd0-9367-1e9595613cfd> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-06T23:51:16.818621Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Mint-gap visibility is the LAST dossier rung, below substrate coverage" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4cd75963-596e-4997-8c4e-1a4ccb92cccc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/df23de4e-800e-4ae6-a170-f17d3b435692> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "v2.2 gate semantics over today's graph" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/e19120a8-38be-4995-b8a4-b2dabdafd0f2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: without the judgment stratum (role/criticality — deferred, AD 7dd7d3c6), the GATE keys honestly on the Constraints already linked in the graph, read via direct_records_for_entity (RecordSummary carries kind, lifecycle status, and the direction-normalized predicate_local, so no separate link walk is needed). Semantics: an entity linked by `violates` to an accepted record → Gate::Deny (the graph asserts an actual violation — the strongest, rarest signal, spec §5.4's tier routed through the gate rather than a new in-editor severity; the Information/Hint LSP ceiling stays untouched); an entity with ≥1 accepted Constraint via `constrains` → Gate::RequireRatification (host 'ask'): a ratified contract governs the entity, but a contract's presence is not proof the edit breaks it, so escalate to a human instead of hard-denying. Anything else → Allow (silence). Non-accepted records (proposed/superseded) never gate. RequirePlan stays in the GateDisposition type but is not emitted — v2.2 has no host-side plan-present signal. Candidate resolution, most precise first: explicit 1-based position → the anchor (the edit's old_string located in the on-disk file, all definitions overlapping its line span) → conservative whole-file scan. Gate precision is therefore bounded by how well Constraints are linked to code entities — the linking discipline (link_code, citation seeds, ratification inbox) is what sharpens the gate over time." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/4d57fbad-f319-4a71-929f-191186e2ba1d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-13T15:52:55.469021Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
