<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/538d7f7a-f432-4164-b417-9f8e03fa552a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "James (owner) ran the approve-spec workflow in trivyn-trial on 2026-08-11, ahead of the Aug-24 novel-affordance boundary set in the 2026-08-09 remediation schedule (ruling 2, incident-2026-08-capture-regression.md), in order to start implementation work on the cloud-tier spec. Confirmed deliberate 2026-08-12; this record is the first-use registration the schedule required, made retroactively the next day.\n\nRegistration data: spec `spec/cloud-tier.md` (trivyn repo; approval marker \"spec-approval: spec/cloud-tier.md\" in trivyn-trial). Event window 2026-08-11T19:46-19:49Z. Records minted, all claude-code-authored: 5 Requirements + 10 Constraints + 10 ArchitecturalDecisions + 1 approval AD = 26. Hub set (Requirement + Constraint) 84 -> 99 (Requirements 42 -> 47, Constraints 42 -> 52); the pre-batch count matches the 2026-08-10 baseline measurement exactly.\n\nEra consequence for the trial readouts: trivyn-trial's restored-era capture (2026-08-10 restoration -> Aug 24 month-2 batch) now contains one enhanced-workflow batch, so month-2/3 capture-quality metrics for trivyn must decompose organic vs spec-batch records (first two days organic-only: isMotivatedBy 3/5 ADs, vs 10/16 with the batch included). moose-trial remains the clean attribution cell for restoration AD c3aa0e1c's P1: no approve-spec use and no CLAUDE.md guidance patch there until after the Aug-24 batch. Boundary rulings for the OTHER pending items (novel capture affordances in tool metadata, retroactive graph repair post-Sep-24) are unchanged by this event." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/538d7f7a-f432-4164-b417-9f8e03fa552a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
