<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Story subject catalog offers only subjects the graph records knowledge about" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/d64ff9bf-c728-44a4-a33c-03c9318a8478> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/8d48edbd-7ee2-4a52-9eac-f2a09c858637> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the Story subject selector browses only subjects the project graph records knowledge about, and a CodeEntity qualifies only when `graph::dossier::code_entities_with_records` — the bulk form of the dossier's `direct_records_for_entity` oracle — finds a dossier-visible record linked to it. Searching still reaches every indexed name; an unrecorded match is returned flagged (`StoryCandidate.no_recorded_knowledge`), sorted after knowledge-bearing subjects, and captioned \"Nothing recorded about this yet\" in the selector.\n\nTHE PROBLEM. The catalog offered every minted code entity: 3,128 subjects, 2,459 of them CodeEntity, of which only 62 had any record linked. A code entity with no record closes over exactly two nodes — itself and the component it realizes — because `expands_story_closure` (src/stories/grounding.rs) expands everything at depth 0 but stops at a SystemComponent hub past it. Measured on the live store: subject `accept_proposal` (recorded) yields 13 evidence items across 5 sections; subject `'& code'0` (a CSS-in-JS object key minted as a CodeEntity) yields 2 and 2. This is Consequence 9fc4f652 of AD ab854392 reaching browse scale — 77% of the catalog was subjects whose Story cannot say anything.\n\nWHERE THE RULE LIVES. The symbolic fact (does the graph record anything here?) is computed server-side from the graph; the visibility policy (hide while browsing, show on search) lives in the selector, which is the only place that knows which state the reader is in — the browse/search distinction Lesson 7039c7f3 already drew for this same selector. The endpoint keeps returning the whole catalog, marked, so any other client can apply its own policy.\n\nWHY THE DOSSIER ORACLE. The first implementation hand-rolled the rule (any predicate, any lifecycle) and diverged within a day: entity `tests` was advertised as knowledge-bearing on the strength of one deprecated record that hover deliberately hides. Sharing `LinkPairs` + `is_dossier_visible` makes browse agree with hover, the dossier, and the why-coverage debt metric (62 → 61), and is also cheaper — one predicate-bound scan per pair instead of one per entity: 262ms → 163ms end to end, helped by skipping the ~2,459 code entities the record walk was probing for record-ness.\n\nJudgments are deliberately excluded, unlike the dossier's silence-rule amendment: a ratified role is a reason for hover to speak, but the Story cannot render one as evidence yet, so counting it would promise evidence the reader never sees." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
