<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6345ceb0-ad2d-4bc1-a4c1-424bcf7f4960> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6345ceb0-ad2d-4bc1-a4c1-424bcf7f4960> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "moose-trial intervention registered: v2 guidance patch + approve-spec on moose-spec.md" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6345ceb0-ad2d-4bc1-a4c1-424bcf7f4960> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6345ceb0-ad2d-4bc1-a4c1-424bcf7f4960> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6345ceb0-ad2d-4bc1-a4c1-424bcf7f4960> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The scheduled post-month-2 intervention on moose-trial, registered BEFORE application (2026-08-26). Sanction chain: incident ruling 2 held novel capture affordances for moose until after the Aug-24 month-2 batch; that batch completed 2026-08-24 and its readout names this intervention — moose capture P1 = 7% (1/14, Aug 10-24), localized to a Requirement-hub deficit (~4 Requirement hubs in store; Pattern a2bf1670 producer gap), not a prompt defect.\n\nTWO PARTS, applied together (staged together in incident report section 11, 2026-08-10): (1) apply `claude-md-v2-guidance.patch` (staged in moose repo 2026-08-10, +25 lines, verified apply-clean 2026-08-26) to moose CLAUDE.md — the four v2 guidance bullets (dossier-before-edit, link_code, concerns/SystemComponent anchoring in its moose-specific no-components variant, NLQ question length) plus the \"Approve a spec before implementing it\" bullet; AGENTS.md is a symlink, so codex sees the same change and moose's control arm changes from this date. (2) Run the approve-spec loop in a moose session against `spec/moose-spec.md` (the early-August spec, still live and mid-implementation) at a re-approval-style gate: extract, dedup, show, gate on explicit yes, mint hubs accepted.\n\nCLEAN-CELL ACCOUNTING (the reason the hold existed): moose-trial was the sole clean attribution cell for the restoration-only P1 read (Consequence 57efbac4). That read is BANKED: month-2 measured restoration-only P1 = 7% — restoration alone does not recover moose capture. This intervention knowingly consumes the clean cell; from the patch date moose capture metrics decompose restored-organic (Aug 10-26) vs intervention-era (Aug 26+), with spec-batch records identifiable by the spec-approval marker and mint timestamps. If v0.11.0 (capture era 3) also deploys before month-3, epoch stamps decompose the binary regime independently of this workflow change.\n\nBASELINE (verified 2026-08-26 from moose-trial kg.nq): 4 accepted Requirements + 21 accepted Constraints = 25 hubs; 0 SystemComponents; 0 spec-approval markers.\n\nFORWARD-SCOPE FENCE (ruling 3 untouched): mint the Requirements/Constraints the spec still governs going forward. NO backfilling isMotivatedBy onto existing records; NO spec-backlog mining; both remain fenced until after the month-3 readout (~Sep 24). SystemComponent minting is NOT improvised mid-run: the store has none and the skill rule is skip-not-invent; if the maintainer chooses to mint the few real components at the gate, that is a deliberate architecture act recorded in the approval AD.\n\nPREDICTION (evaluable month-3, on its face, per symmetric-commitment AD 4aa634b8): with hubs available, new claude-code ADs on moose recover isMotivatedBy >= 50% (the c3aa0e1c P1 bar, Jun band). If hubs exist and P1 still fails at month-3, the workflow hypothesis is wrong and low linkage is read as real — no new mechanism stories. Kill thresholds (Constraint 75b0cf14) untouched.\n\nPOST-RUN OBLIGATION (the 406b05f7 per-use data block): same-day Consequence on this record carrying records minted by kind, hub delta, approval-marker path, and event window.\n\nFollows AD 406b05f7 (approve-spec first-use pattern + per-use registration discipline)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
