<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/768665cb-8f3a-4a9b-b89b-b83903050dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/768665cb-8f3a-4a9b-b89b-b83903050dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: Story uses one deterministic backend planner for both instant and curated subsystem narratives. The planner resolves a SystemComponent, selects a bounded three-to-five-beat route from current accepted graph records and code anchors, and derives structured checks symbolically. A configured LLM is strongly recommended to turn that closed evidence set into concise human prose; symbolic extractive rendering is the fallback. Generated runs are ephemeral unless saved. Saved draft and published recipes are typed, version-controlled project files outside the knowledge graph and contain only the subject, learning goal, ordered beat intents, record IRIs, code symbols, status, and curator metadata. The workbench is a thin client of daemon-owned planning, validation, persistence, and grading." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/768665cb-8f3a-4a9b-b89b-b83903050dea> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
