<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "First-class Requirements UI uses reusable artifact service" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "First-class Requirements UI renders Requirement records through a reusable backend artifact service, following the established ADR artifact-service precedent. The implementation adds a read-only requirements renderer that counts and enumerates Requirement records, renders generated markdown detail pages, reports linkage warnings, and summarizes inbound ArchitecturalDecision isMotivatedBy links. Thin REST endpoints expose list, detail, and ZIP archive responses. The React UI adds a Requirements page and shared markdown IRI navigation so Requirement IRIs in ADRs open the corresponding requirement, and ArchitecturalDecision IRIs in requirement details open the corresponding ADR. The project graph remains the source of truth; the feature does not write generated docs." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T04:02:52.157996Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "First-class Requirements UI uses reusable artifact service" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/12dcb29d-d40d-4b7e-92c9-8140a155a732> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/6e83b84e-bce2-4c21-9ca6-fa3e96480928> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/899b9ab9-f670-4025-bb26-1c9d046fde01> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#resultsIn> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/a509703d-3ed6-411d-8aad-38ad6c270f0a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Benchmark model suite spans the capability spectrum" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Four models span the capability spectrum the value thesis lives on: (1) codex-spark (strong frontier, codex CLI) — efficiency regime; recovers code-rule knowledge by exploration. (2) Sonnet (claude-sonnet-4-6, claude -p) — second strong anchor in a different family/harness (generalization). (3) Haiku (claude-haiku-4-5, claude -p) — the TRANSITION PROBE: small but HOSTED, so an accuracy lift (not just efficiency) would be a reproducible capability win without local infra; and because it pulls reliably it isolates the capability axis from the delivery/pull-gap axis. (4) A3B (qwen3.6-35b-a3b, opencode + LM Studio) — the weak/self-hosted anchor where memory becomes a capability win AND the pull gap appears (won't call the tool, so push is necessary). Skipped: gemma (weaker 2nd local, can't co-load with A3B) and Opus (redundant strong anchor).\n\nHARNESS MAPPING (multi-harness): Claude models -> Claude Code headless (claude -p); codex-spark -> codex CLI; A3B -> opencode + LM Studio. claude -p is a complete harness for Claude models: --mcp-config attaches the moosedev MCP (B2) and the free-text recall MCP (B1-rag); --output-format json yields per-run input/output/CACHE tokens, total_cost_usd, num_turns, duration, and the resolved model id (cleaner than parsing opencode logs); --append-system-prompt carries arm guidance and the push/oracle injection. Retained from the superseded decision: memory is injected as an MCP server so B1/B2 differ only in representation.\n\nACCOUNTING RULE (caching): claude -p uses prompt caching, so its raw token totals are NOT comparable to the no-cache local (opencode/LM Studio) runs (cf. the token-fingerprint gap). Headline efficiency metric = the WITHIN-model cold-vs-push token RATIO (cache/harness-robust); keep absolute counts harness-tagged.\n\nCOMPARISON NOTE: pull-reliability is harness-dependent (Lesson 094087c7 — pull fails for local across opencode AND codex), so the cross-model comparison leans on the harness-independent push/oracle arm; tooluse/pull shows the per-harness pull gap (esp. A3B). Iterate task design on cheap/fast Haiku+Sonnet, add slow local A3B for the final capability runs." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/280c1722-9f41-4488-954c-333bec2c56ca> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T18:00:02.317673Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Benchmark model suite spans the capability spectrum (codex-spark / Sonnet / Haiku / A3B), run per-harness; within-model token-ratio is the efficiency metric" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8b48ab85-cf38-4925-a73a-ea3c21e23842> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/f45cf655-2dc7-4b29-b93d-b3c62c8517d0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8dd7da0c-5630-4119-8495-18d5dd31909c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8dd7da0c-5630-4119-8495-18d5dd31909c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Observation stratum: git-derived churn lives in a derived sidecar, not the KG" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8dd7da0c-5630-4119-8495-18d5dd31909c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8dd7da0c-5630-4119-8495-18d5dd31909c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8dd7da0c-5630-4119-8495-18d5dd31909c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the observation stratum's first signals — per-file churn (commit count in a 24-month window, last-commit recency) and authorship concentration (distinct authors, top-author share) — are stored as a derived cache (.moosedev/substrate/churn.json, own schema_version, anchored to indexed_commit) rebuilt by `moosedev index` alongside the SCIP substrate, NOT as append-only Observation nodes in the project graph. Why: git already IS the append-only, commit-anchored, shared, versioned ledger these metrics derive from — a fresh clone reproduces churn.json bit-for-bit by running the same `moosedev index` it already needs for the substrate, so there is nothing to track, share, or retain; kg.nq stays a reviewable file of ratified knowledge rather than growing measurement rows every index run; and spec open question #4 (observation retention/rollup policy) dissolves for git-derived metrics. The parked ontology classes Observation, CodeSnapshot, and AuthorshipProvenance remain parked: their honest writers are true instrumentation (perf profiles, defect attribution) that is not derivable from an existing ledger — those enter the graph in a later slice with the retention policy question addressed then. The epistemic line: judgments (human-ratified interpretive claims like role/criticality) go to kg.nq; measurements derivable from git are recomputed locally and never stored as truth anywhere. Consumers (dossier/hover observations digest per spec §5.3 item 4, the classifier's evidence) read the sidecar at query time via Substrate::churn_for_file. This is a conscious amendment of spec §3.4's letter (stratum-3 rows in the graph), sanctioned by James 2026-07-13 during slice planning. Distinct from but consistent with the fires.jsonl-outside-KG precedent (AD 305f87a8: operational data is not knowledge)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/8dd7da0c-5630-4119-8495-18d5dd31909c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
