<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Whole-file module occurrences are not position hits" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/889e6b24-de43-4786-b592-ae057aad54f1> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "phase7-acceptance" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Substrate::resolve skips any Module-kind occurrence that starts at 0:0 and spans multiple lines (is_synthetic_whole_file_marker) - rust-analyzer emits these as whole-file containers for every file, not as tokens. Token-less positions (comments, blank lines) therefore miss honestly instead of resolving to the enclosing module; modules stay reachable via their mod declaration name token, SCIP symbol, or entity IRI. Generalizes AD 77b7f5f7 (which filtered only the crate/ marker) to all per-file module symbols; resolves the 2026-07-08 slice-2 acceptance finding where a comment line in a module-linked file surfaced the module dossier and a mistyped link_code position could silently link the whole module. The multi-line requirement is what keeps real module name tokens (always single-line) resolvable; ingestion and definitions() are untouched, so module entities remain mintable." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-09T14:40:20.782062Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Whole-file module occurrences are not position hits" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/17b33064-170f-4838-a351-811aa7b143e6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab379ef4-e43c-457b-ab4b-e51fe68a450d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/ff00bb2d-ef36-4797-ac7a-7feaa594e13e> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Story code anchors stop at the subject for CodeEntity subjects" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/d4b7175e-fd11-4709-9ef6-1f44f6d7af49> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: `entity_code` (src/stories/grounding.rs) now takes a `ComponentExpansion` choice — a CodeEntity subject gets `SubjectOnly`, every other entity subject keeps `Full`. Previously any neighboring current SystemComponent was expanded into its ENTIRE code listing, for every subject kind. Why: membership in a component is not relevance to the subject. `propose_link` (one function in src/graph/proposals.rs) neighbors the graph/store layer, so its Story inhaled all of src/graph/** — 512 anchors across 26 files, hitting the MAX_STORY_ENTITIES cap, listing `canonical`, `WriteThrottle`, `StartupAction` and other entities with nothing to do with the subject. A CodeEntity subject already names its own position precisely; the component's other members are siblings, not anchors. A record (ArchitecturalDecision, Lesson, …) frequently has no code of its own, so the component it concerns is its only available grounding — those keep expanding. Measured on the real store, same subject, assist_level 1: anchors 512 → 1 (`propose_link · src/graph/proposals.rs:221`), max citations per paragraph 150 → 3, narration coverage 519 eligible/truncated → 8 eligible/not truncated. No regression: a SystemComponent story still lists 512 anchors (correct — it is a story ABOUT that layer, and all 512 are in its evidence), and an AD story keeps 427 anchors with 0 unresolved citations. Reported by James 2026-08-16 (\"having a hard time believing those are all relevant\")." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-16T19:36:35.042011Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Story code anchors stop at the subject for CodeEntity subjects" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isMotivatedBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/9327d3b1-d868-4f37-9d0d-eb7ee3f054de> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
