<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ab854392-2aab-4273-ac2e-c2eba33f1cca> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/f10d855f-e7ac-4ed6-a83a-a381593e562a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ADR set memo keyed on the project write generation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/552e6950-34af-4fa2-b93e-18d381c2a4ba> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "opencode-moosedev" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: GET /adrs (and /adrs/{num}, /adrs/archive.zip) serve a memoized AdrSet — AppState.adr_memo holds (write_generation, options, Arc<AdrSet>); generate_adr_set_cached returns the Arc while project_write_generation() and options match, else regenerates under the memo lock (single-flight). Rendering walks every decision cluster (~40ms/ADR, 0.73s for this repo), so per-request regeneration made the workbench ADR tab feel broken; warm reads now cost ~0.7ms. This is a derived cache, not a second brain: the memo lives IN the daemon, memoizes a deterministic function of the store, and is invalidated exactly by the store own write counter — the same signal the LSP diagnostics refresh already trusts (Constraint 2ba76439 forbids SURFACES growing their own indexes/policy, which this is not). Named invariant it leans on: every project-graph write path must call note_project_write() — true today for MCP tools, the proposal queue, grounded capture, taxonomy seeding, and HTTP graph import; CLI writers (mint/classify) run with the daemon stopped. A future write path that skips the bump would serve stale ADRs AND stale LSP diagnostics — the shared signal keeps both honest or both wrong, never silently divergent." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-14T20:13:29.968614Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "ADR set memo keyed on the project write generation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/ae3aa72c-55dd-413c-a554-83ffe0e516eb> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/065f3a0c-8ffc-4d84-9401-cf43a6051afc> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b0d3e4d9-873c-4b5b-bff1-0403c6ab1724> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b0d3e4d9-873c-4b5b-bff1-0403c6ab1724> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Code-layer ontology: three strata with distinct change-semantics" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b0d3e4d9-873c-4b5b-bff1-0403c6ab1724> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b0d3e4d9-873c-4b5b-bff1-0403c6ab1724> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the v2 code layer is organized as three ontological strata with different authorities and lifecycles. (1) STRUCTURE — rigid, derived deterministically from source at every commit, never hand-asserted: containment as TWO hierarchies kept distinct (logical crate/module/item AND physical directory/file, crossed by declaredIn); kind (function/method/type/trait/macro/const/test/migration/config); topology (calls/uses/implements/accesses/testedBy, with derived fan-in/out and blast radius); exposure (public API, FFI, network entry points). (2) JUDGMENTS — anti-rigid, proposed from evidence, human-ratified, lifecycle-managed: role (per AD b5b4762b: core-algorithm/domain-logic/boundary/glue/boilerplate/generated); CRITICALITY as an axis ORTHOGONAL to role (a payments CRUD handler is boilerplate by role, critical by cost-of-being-wrong); attention policy = f(role, criticality, observations), never f(role) alone; domain-concept links; contracts, which REUSE the existing Constraint class with constrains widened to code entities. (3) OBSERVATIONS — measured occurrents, append-only, instrument-provenanced, commit-anchored: performance, change dynamics (churn/age/authorship concentration → per-region bus factor), defect attribution, verification state, and authorship provenance (human vs which agent/session — first-class in the agent era; likely reuses the existing provenance named-graph machinery). Ontological discipline (OntoClean): rigid kind vs anti-rigid role — an entity IS a Function and PLAYS CoreAlgorithm via a playsRole relation carrying status + provenance, never a subclass. Mixing strata in one categorization destroys knowing which facts are re-derivable vs ratified (e.g. \"interface\" is largely structural/derivable via the existing Interface/exposes; \"core algorithm\" is a judgment). ALIGNMENT PASS (2026-07-03): all 8 candidate terms (CodeEntity, CodeSnapshot, CodeRole, Criticality, AttentionPolicy, Observation, AuthorshipProvenance, CodeFile) returned ambiguous below thresholds (top cosines 0.46–0.54 vs 0.55 bar) — genuinely new vocabulary, no false merges; mint in the software-engineering ontology under the Component/Module lineage (CodeEntity's top candidate: SystemComponent 0.488). Confirmed REUSES, not re-mints: Interface, InterfaceDefinition, Module, DataStore, Constraint, the supersession/lifecycle machinery, dependsOn/implements/uses/accesses/exposes." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b0d3e4d9-873c-4b5b-bff1-0403c6ab1724> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/b0d3e4d9-873c-4b5b-bff1-0403c6ab1724> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-03T22:17:54.01551Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
