<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c3aa0e1c-55fe-4b66-8742-6f24d82149d6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MCP metadata contract, amended: instruction and worked examples are load-bearing" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c3aa0e1c-55fe-4b66-8742-6f24d82149d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c3aa0e1c-55fe-4b66-8742-6f24d82149d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c3aa0e1c-55fe-4b66-8742-6f24d82149d6> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Tool descriptions must carry imperative capture instruction and worked relation examples, not only routing and side-effect metadata. The original contract (ee900bdb) correctly established MCP metadata as an operational routing contract — distinguish adjacent tools, expose side effects, encode the get_relevant_context → query → sparql ladder — and all of that stands and is retained. What it left unstated, and what its implementation in commit 4486358 (2026-07-16) removed, is that these same strings are the only place an agent is told WHICH typed links to assert, and whether to trust recall over re-deriving from source. Restored under this amendment: (a) the imperative capture-cluster instruction on record_important_decision (\"record what you actually weighed; omit when there is none — do not invent\"); (b) worked relation examples on relate and suggest_links, including \"an ArchitecturalDecision isMotivatedBy a Requirement\" and the under-linked-scan example; (c) the get_relevant_context TRUST clause (\"prefer its recorded answer over re-deriving from the code\"). EVIDENCE: isMotivatedBy coverage on new ArchitecturalDecisions in the moose-trial store fell 52% (wk of Jul 13) → 14% (wk of Jul 20) → 3% (wk of Jul 27) → 3% (Aug) — a step change at 4486358, not a drift. The converse experiment: alternatives_considered shipped in 622d525 (2026-06-26) and weighs coverage went 0-3% across four prior months → 86% within two weeks, with no change in who was doing the work. PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION: isMotivatedBy returns to >=50% on new claude-code-authored ArchitecturalDecisions after this lands; baseline to beat is 3%; measured by SPARQL filtering hasTimestamp > the restore commit and hasAuthor = claude-code. This is registered step 1 of 2: the novel affordances (rationale parameter, length advisory, capture-time dedup) are deliberately withheld until after the in-anger trial's month-2 batch (2026-08-24) so recovery attribution stays clean, and no record captured after 2026-07-16 is corrected until post-trial." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
