<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c94e50a6-d82b-4e70-b949-528c18067304> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c94e50a6-d82b-4e70-b949-528c18067304> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c94e50a6-d82b-4e70-b949-528c18067304> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the CodeEntity record page became source-aware and the LSP hover gained a Story link, entirely through runtime projections of the current substrate — no new route family, no new ontology term, and no graph write.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED.\n1. ONE location helper. `Substrate::definition_location(symbol)` resolves a symbol to its defining file AND definition range through the same SCIP/tree-sitter ladder `definition_for_symbol` uses. It probes a memoized normalized-symbol map: symbols read back out of the graph are version-normalized (Constraint `00b3986e`) while the index holds raw ones, so the naive miss path normalized every indexed symbol on EVERY lookup — quadratic, and enough to stall Story generation outright. Collisions resolve exactly as minting does (scope first via the shared `is_test_path`, then lowest (file, symbol)), because anything else resolves a minted entity to the definition minting dropped.\n2. `GET /api/v1/records/{uuid}` gained an optional `code` block, and `GET /api/v1/records/{uuid}/source?scope=context|full` serves bounded, trusted text. Availability is decided from metadata alone; one pinned `Arc<Substrate>` serves both the location and the read, so coordinates and bytes can never come from different generations. Caps drop whole lines, a single oversized line is cut on a character boundary, peak allocation is bounded by the window rather than the file, and a definition that does not fit inside the returned text is refused rather than advertised.\n3. Trust is inherited, not reinvented: the generation-proven read AD `ec521d7d` built for LSP coordinates is the same gate the HTTP surface uses. The unit of proof is the FILE — see Constraint `0c6e01ff` for the full rule, including symlink containment and the address-literal `Host` requirement that closes DNS rebinding.\n4. The WebUI renders a code section above the relationship graph: kind, signature, symbol, path, a line-numbered preview with definition lines marked (end-exclusive), and a full-file expansion that preserves the working preview if it fails — plain monospace, escaped text, no syntax-highlighting dependency.\n5. `#/stories/entity/{uuid}` is the canonical Story deep link, emitted only for slash-addressable IRIs the record route can actually resolve. \"Tell this Story\" on a CodeEntity names the entity itself rather than its containing component.\n6. The hover carries `[Tell me the Story]` under its identity block via `render_dossier_markdown(dossier, story_url)`, using the live published HTTP address and omitting the link when the workbench is not serving.\n7. Story `code_anchors` carry their current definition line, published only when the file baseline is provable, and paired with the path they were resolved in.\n\nWHY THIS SHAPE. Canonical UUID routing already governs every record, so specializing the existing `#/record/{uuid}` destination keeps one deep link per subject. Making a Story destination refreshable turned navigation into genuinely concurrent state — in-flight generation, deep-link resolution, history traversal, and the dirty-editor guard — and most of the review's findings landed there rather than in the substrate." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
