<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c9874c4c-2e76-41a2-b376-f431f7478c2b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/c9874c4c-2e76-41a2-b376-f431f7478c2b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the CodeEntity record page becomes source-aware and the LSP hover gains a Story link, entirely through runtime projections of the current substrate — no new route family, no new ontology term, and no graph write.\n\nWHAT WAS BUILT.\n1. ONE location helper. `Substrate::definition_location(symbol)` resolves a symbol to its defining file AND definition range through the same SCIP/tree-sitter ladder `definition_for_symbol` already uses; the tree-sitter side generalized `identity_alive` into an `identity_location` that returns the declaration's range. Every surface that needs \"where is this defined\" goes through it, so no surface can locate code by searching a file for its name.\n2. `GET /api/v1/records/{uuid}` gains an optional `code` block, and `GET /api/v1/records/{uuid}/source?scope=context|full` serves bounded, trusted text (context = definition ±12 lines, 400 lines / 256 KiB; full = 20,000 lines / 1 MiB). Caps drop WHOLE lines, so the reported `start_line`/`end_line` always describe the text returned and the payload stays UTF-8 valid without a boundary search. Public coordinates are 1-based.\n3. Source is admitted only through `read_indexed_source`, so a stale index or an edited working tree yields metadata plus a reindex explanation and no preview. The route also refuses a cross-origin `Origin` while serving same-origin and Origin-less local callers.\n4. The WebUI renders a code section above the relationship graph: kind, signature, symbol, path, a line-numbered preview with definition lines marked, and a full-file expansion — plain monospace, escaped text, no syntax-highlighting dependency.\n5. `#/stories/entity/{uuid}` is the canonical Story deep link; \"Tell this Story\" on a CodeEntity now names the entity itself rather than its containing component, and routes through the hash so the destination is refreshable.\n6. The hover carries `[Tell me the Story]` under its identity block via a new `render_dossier_markdown(dossier, story_url)`, using the live published HTTP address and omitting the link when the workbench is not serving.\n7. Story `code_anchors` get their current definition line from the same helper, resolved for the rendered anchors only.\n\nWHY THIS SHAPE. Canonical UUID routing already governs every record, so specializing the existing `#/record/{uuid}` destination keeps one deep link per subject. Trust is inherited rather than reinvented: the generation-proven read that AD ec521d7d built for LSP coordinates is the same gate the HTTP surface uses, so both surfaces go quiet under exactly the same conditions." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
