<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "v2.3 spec amendment: Record-constraint and Mark-rationale-stale code actions deferred" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: of spec §5.6's four editor code actions, v2.3 ships the three that fit the ratification queue cleanly — \"Link decision to this entity…\" (suggested candidates), \"Propose role: <r>\", \"Propose criticality: high|low\" — and DEFERS \"Record constraint…\" and \"Mark rationale stale\" past v2.3 (user-sanctioned 2026-07-13). Why: both are blocked on a workbench compose/edit surface, not on the queue. \"Record constraint…\" needs free text, and a bare LSP session has no input surface (the session deliberately has no server→client request plumbing — client responses are dropped at the read loop — and the workbench has no record-compose form). \"Mark rationale stale\" additionally lacks a persisted review mechanism: staleness today is a COMPUTED hint (newest linked record predates the file's last commit) that self-heals when the record is updated or superseded; a persisted human flag is a new workflow concept needing clearing semantics — it cannot ride hasLifecycleStatus (a record can be accepted AND need review), and without a clearing story the flag itself rots, the exact comprehension-debt failure mode MOOSEDev exists to fight. The ontology edit itself is trivial (~10 lines TTL + a shapes branch) — the missing piece is review-workflow design, so the honest version is its own follow-up slice alongside a compose surface." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-14T07:31:16.96279Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "v2.3 spec amendment: Record-constraint and Mark-rationale-stale code actions deferred" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/306e9609-93bc-4d96-8d2c-5b8e17ccf19d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d0925fc7-13f2-4368-9014-64059dc4343a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#weighs> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Alternative/7a67468f-892f-4775-bd92-37b91a8a4404> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "scip-typescript visibility: positive declaration-suffix gate" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/7e46131e-50cc-4b86-9207-e0aeb116745d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a SCIP symbol is a top-level declaration when its ancestor descriptors are all Namespace AND its last descriptor is declaration-forming — Type (`#`), Term (`.`), Method (`().`), or Macro (`!`). Namespace, Meta (`:`), Parameter, and TypeParameter are rejected. The gate is defined by what a descriptor IS, not by what it is not, so a descriptor kind nobody enumerated cannot leak through.\n\nWHY POSITIVE. The superseded formulation (`!is_namespace(last)`) is a double negative over an open set: every SCIP suffix except Namespace passed, including kinds that did not exist in the authors' mental model. The allowlist closes the set. This is the same shape of fix as the ontology-IRI rule (Constraint 19bb4d8a): enumerate what is admissible, never what is excluded.\n\nEMPIRICAL CLOSURE, verified against the producers' own descriptor tables rather than by reasoning. scip-typescript (FileIndexer.ts:527-580) emits Meta from exactly three constructs — typeReference, typeLiteral, propertyAssignment — none of which is a declaration; interface/enum/type-alias/class are Type, function/method/constructor/accessor are Method, property/enum-member/variable declarations are Term, `namespace X` is Package (== Namespace, same discriminant). scip-python has exactly two metaDescriptor call sites: the `pkg/__init__:` module marker, which lang/python.rs canonicalizes to a Namespace at ingest before this gate ever sees it, and a degenerate parentless fallback. Neither producer emits Macro; rust-analyzer does (`impl_story_error!`), and Rust does not route through this gate today, so Macro is included for forward-compatibility rather than current need. On this project's live TS index the allowlist keeps 313 true top-level declarations (140 Method, 127 Type, 46 Term) and drops 1,476 Meta.\n\nWHAT ELSE CHANGED. `names_an_identifier` is deleted, not kept as belt-and-braces. It is fully subsumed — among top-level Type/Term/Method/Macro symbols in the live index, zero have non-identifier names — and it is actively harmful: it rejects `<constructor>` and `<get>`-prefixed accessor descriptors and TS 4.5 arbitrary module namespace names (`export { x as \"foo bar\" }`), all genuine declarations. Its unit test asserted on a symbol shape scip-typescript never emits (a Term `.` tail where all 47 real quoted keys in the index end in `:`), which is how the bug survived a guard written specifically for it. scip-typescript is left with the plain contract: non-local AND top-level declaration.\n\nUNCHANGED. Export-ness is still not encoded by scip-typescript 0.4.0, so this remains a documented over-approximation: private top-level declarations still batch-mint. Python keeps its PEP 8 underscore rule; Rust still keys on the rendered `pub` signature prefix and does not use this predicate. Placement follows AD 6fc36a85 — the suffix allowlist is a grammar-generic symbol helper and stays in symbols.rs; TypeScript-specific policy, ground-truth citations, and test fixtures stay in lang/typescript.rs." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d132b7c8-3efb-48a8-b0c0-9a528474d18c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ff3f4751-7bc7-4f93-8149-c6858368f6ea> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
