<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d1e04b46-ff2e-419d-be2f-7f0e4cb6a76d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/f4d2f589-8f00-4640-ae16-fbb0184cb365> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d1e04b46-ff2e-419d-be2f-7f0e4cb6a76d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d1e04b46-ff2e-419d-be2f-7f0e4cb6a76d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Story v3 replaces beat-card planning with a deterministic typed dossier for SystemComponent, InformationRecord, CodeEntity, and bounded Topic subjects. The dossier contains the subject's direct typed neighborhood, complete supersession graph, record clusters, timestamps, lifecycle, code anchors, and explicit gaps. The reader shows a brief, one cohesive cited account with light headings, a deterministic chronology, an evidence appendix, gaps, and symbolic checks. Recipes store subject, goal, include/exclude references, section emphasis, and curator context. LLM assistance receives only dossier-derived evidence: a single validated synthesis when it fits, otherwise a bounded citation-preserving map/reduce pipeline; all failures retain the symbolic account. The workbench remains a thin client and Story activity never writes project knowledge." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
