<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d3d4d7b1-a904-4519-98d8-31a24bffa125> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d3d4d7b1-a904-4519-98d8-31a24bffa125> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Validate MOOSEDev via a longitudinal in-anger trial on trivyn + moose" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d3d4d7b1-a904-4519-98d8-31a24bffa125> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d3d4d7b1-a904-4519-98d8-31a24bffa125> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Decision (2026-06-23): validate MOOSEDev's core thesis — reducing comprehension debt — by USING it in anger on trivyn and moose, the maintainer's actively-developed projects, over ~the next few months (through ~Q3 2026). RATIONALE: the multi-corpus benchmark phase established TWO demonstrable structural wins — (1) capability: completeness/negation/supersession/multi-hop over large typed sets, structured graph (B2) categorically beats flat RAG (B1), reproduced on private trivyn AND public codegraph; (2) currency/anti-staleness (graph serves the current decision; free-text is currency-blind) — plus a pile of HONEST NULLS (retrieval ≈ parity with good RAG; no scale-compounding; decomposition saturates on clean corpora; efficiency modest, not the pre-registered <20%). The ACTUAL motivating thesis — that structured memory reduces the slow loss of *why* a codebase is shaped as it is, over months — remains UNMEASURED; only a longitudinal in-anger trial can earn it. RISK to guard: a self-run trial is prone to confirmation bias (the builder will 'see it working'). To yield EVIDENCE not anecdote it must be instrumented UP FRONT: (a) a pre-registered comprehension-debt signal — a fixed set of 'recover the why of decision X' probes re-scored monthly, with vs without the graph; (b) a running tally of when the graph actually saved a re-derivation in real work (or was bypassed); (c) a pre-registered kill/abandon condition (e.g., 'if I'm not reaching for it unprompted by month 2'); optionally (d) a hold-out (keep moose's graph deliberately behind, or leave some decisions uncaptured, for contrast). Side benefit: dogfooding hardens the capture + bootstrap workflow on real projects. Outward claims (blog/social) must stay scoped to what's demonstrated — this trial is the path to claiming more, not a claim itself." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d3d4d7b1-a904-4519-98d8-31a24bffa125> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d3d4d7b1-a904-4519-98d8-31a24bffa125> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T08:02:29.719041Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d3d4d7b1-a904-4519-98d8-31a24bffa125> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Validate MOOSEDev via a longitudinal in-anger trial on trivyn + moose" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Always-mint scope: modules plus the public non-member surface" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/3aef1247-0774-43d0-98d9-ecb344e876de> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/b787c62d-3dca-4102-87d4-ebdc8bc93549> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: `moosedev mint` creates CodeEntity nodes for modules, and for non-test definitions that are both publicly visible AND declarations in their own right rather than members of another declaration. Private items and members enter the graph only when `link_code` attaches knowledge to them.\n\nTHE TWO AXES. Visibility is per-language and lives in the `lang/` producer hooks (`ProducerHooks::is_public`): rust-analyzer keys on the rendered `pub` signature prefix, scip-typescript on the structural declaration gate (AD d132b7c8), scip-python on that gate plus the PEP 8 underscore convention. Unit-hood is grammar-generic and lives in `graph::code_entities::is_type_member`, keyed on the SCIP `SymbolInformation.Kind` the substrate already carries. Both must hold. Modules bypass both and mint through the `is_module` path as before.\n\nWHY MEMBERS ARE EXCLUDED. A `pub` field is public API by visibility, and the visibility gate is right to admit it. But nobody records an architectural decision about a field: the reason it exists is the reason its type exists, and that rationale attaches to the type. Minting one entity per field produced 759 permanently silent anchors here. Excluding them from BATCH minting does not make them unlinkable — it is exactly the treatment private items already get, and `link_code` still lazily mints any field that turns out to carry its own invariant. That path is not hypothetical: of the two fields that did hold a record, `alternatives_considered` was retained by the prune for precisely this reason.\n\nONE PREDICATE, BOTH CONSUMERS. `is_type_member` is consulted by `mint_candidates` and by `is_debt_surface` together, deliberately. Splitting them — counting fields as debt while refusing to mint entities for them — would make the metric measure documentation that no entity could ever hold, and would reintroduce the drift between mint scope and debt surface that keeps the two honest. Every definition the metric counts is one an entity exists for.\n\nEVIDENCE (2026-08-19). Applying the rule moved 745 minted field entities into `MintPlan::out_of_scope`; the prune removed 743 of them (10,402 quads across the project and provenance graphs) and retained 21 under its conjuncts — 20 with subject-side knowledge edges and one, `is_public`, referenced object-side by a Lesson. Catalog 1,723 to 981. Why-coverage 26/1,739 (1.50%) to 26/928 (2.80%). Full suite 502 passed; SHACL conforms with 0 violations. Skipped-scope rose 3,547 to 4,542, which is where fields are now counted.\n\nUNCHANGED FROM THE SUPERSEDED RECORD. Test paths are still skipped wholesale. Private items still lazy-mint. Previously minted IRIs remain stable by normalized SCIP symbol, so this narrowing severed no record-to-entity link — the prune's second conjunct exists to guarantee that, and it is what retained all 21." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d52505d4-69c1-4e1f-8ece-a2f97f3e917b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
