<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d699f118-f608-4840-93de-81f434bbf97b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: post-v2 editor expansion delivers VS Code and Emacs as pure client registrations over the unchanged Knowledge-LSP, confirming spec §5.7's one-server/thin-clients bet — the July 2026 capability research found every feature the server uses (full-sync, hover, codeLens, codeAction, executeCommand, pull+push diagnostics, showMessage, showDocument, positionEncoding, initializationOptions) is plain LSP 3.17 in all four target clients. VS Code (clients/vscode): an LSP-client-only extension (~110 LOC TypeScript, esbuild bundle, local .vsix via vsce; marketplace out of scope) that launches `moosedev lsp` with cwd = the .moosedev workspace folder (cwd is load-bearing — the autospawned daemon derives repo root from it), sets diagnosticPullOptions {onChange, onSave} (the languageclient default only pulls on open), maps moosedev.* settings to the server's initializationOptions shape with restart-on-change, and registers NO commands (vscode-languageclient auto-registers server-advertised executeCommand ids); VS Code negotiates UTF-16 only (vscode-languageserver-node #1224) and the server's fallback covers it. `moosedev init --vscode` seeds .vscode/settings.json, parallel to --zed. Emacs (clients/emacs/moosedev.el): ONE file carrying both registrations — eglot (built-in, zero-install baseline; entry APPENDED to eglot-server-programs so it never shadows the language server) and lsp-mode (:add-on? t so MOOSEDev co-resides with the language server; the only Emacs path with code lenses — eglot has none, GNU bug#73452). Version floors documented: pull diagnostics eglot≥1.20 / lsp-mode≥10 (older clients keep the push path), UTF-8 eglot≥1.12 / lsp-mode≥10 / Neovim 0.11." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
