<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e43baa99-7ced-4e24-a526-f5aa9cb2235b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#ArchitecturalDecision> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e43baa99-7ced-4e24-a526-f5aa9cb2235b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "One project root serves configuration and every repository-scoped operation" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e43baa99-7ced-4e24-a526-f5aa9cb2235b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e43baa99-7ced-4e24-a526-f5aa9cb2235b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e43baa99-7ced-4e24-a526-f5aa9cb2235b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e43baa99-7ced-4e24-a526-f5aa9cb2235b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the project an invocation belongs to is computed ONCE, in `src/project.rs`, and used both for `.env` discovery and for every repository-scoped operation — index, mint, classify, resolve, LSP path mapping, the reindex scheduler, and the daemon's substrate load. Deriving them separately is not a tidiness issue; it silently corrupts the store.\n\nTHE FAILURE IT PREVENTS. 0.7.1 began anchoring relative `.env` paths to the file's own directory, so `MOOSEDEV_DATA_DIR=.moosedev` names the project's store rather than a directory under wherever the process started. But the repo root stayed `std::env::current_dir()` at ten call sites. A run from `project/src` would then load `project/.moosedev` and hand rust-analyzer `project/src` — publishing a substrate covering one subdirectory into the whole project's store, where nothing downstream can tell it is partial. Before the anchoring the two were wrong in the same direction and therefore consistent; fixing one alone is what made them disagree.\n\nSHAPE. `project_root()` walks up from the working directory to the nearest ancestor carrying a marker (`.git`, or any supported language's manifest), falling back to the working directory. `.env` discovery uses the same walk, stopping at that root so it can never reach `$HOME`. The markers live here rather than being shared with the substrate producers' language detection, which answers a stricter and unrelated question — TypeScript demands `tsconfig.json` AND `package.json` before an indexer will run, which is the wrong test for \"where does this project keep its configuration\".\n\nNO BUILD-TIME FALLBACK. The `.env` search deliberately has no `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` entry. That path is baked in at compile time, so a dev build run in a project with no `.env` of its own would load MOOSEDev's — its data dir AND its LLM credentials — and, with anchoring, resolve that store back to MOOSEDev's own directory, writing another project's work into MOOSEDev's graph. Inside the MOOSEDev repo the ordinary walk finds the same file, so the fallback only ever reached cases where it was wrong.\n\nFound by code review, 2026-08-06, after the anchoring change; regression-locked by `src/project.rs` unit tests plus the dotenv-candidate tests in `main.rs`." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
