<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb61ce61-63f8-446d-8603-3f424f4d11d8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: the v2.3 editor write path needs NO server→client requests — the codeAction menu IS the selection UI. textDocument/codeAction returns one fully-formed CodeAction per choice (per candidate record from the hybrid-seeded link_candidates search, per role, per criticality), each carrying a Command; the client invokes workspace/executeCommand (moosedev.proposeLink | moosedev.proposeJudgment), which arrives as an ordinary request in the existing single-threaded dispatch chain and files a proposal into the ratification queue via propose_link/propose_judgment — the session's ONLY write path (Constraint 2ba76439: no side doors; auditable via `grep -nE 'link_code|relate\\(|accept_proposal|reject_proposal|ensure_entity|record_instance|store\\.insert|txn\\.insert|start_transaction|mint_' src/lsp/` returning nothing, made executable by tests/lsp_write_path.rs's source-scan test). Actions use CodeActionKind QUICKFIX — a custom moosedev.* kind would be silently filtered by clients that send context.only; the semantic-purity loss is accepted. Menu discipline: silence mirrors hover (no substrate resolution, local symbol, or no workspace definition → no lightbulb); link candidates cap at 4, exclude already-linked records and records with a pending link proposal for the symbol; a judgment axis with ANY live judgment (proposed or ratified) is suppressed entirely (maxCount 1 makes a second edge unratifiable); criticality `standard` is the implicit default and never offered. Editor-originated judgments are human assertions — confidence 1.0, ESCALATED, author `editor:<clientInfo.name slugified>` — but STILL proposals ratified in the workbench, never auto-accepted; and they never nudge (pending_count excludes judgments), accepted because the inbox shows them escalated-first. propose_judgment gained the same pending-twin dedup guard propose_link had, so repeated editor invocations and classifier re-runs are idempotent." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fb61ce61-63f8-446d-8603-3f424f4d11d8> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
