<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ae8fa7b-350f-4f7c-9840-0f32dee8257a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Describing a CodeEntity costs metadata for indexed symbols, one bounded parse for syntactic ones" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ae8fa7b-350f-4f7c-9840-0f32dee8257a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ae8fa7b-350f-4f7c-9840-0f32dee8257a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Describing a CodeEntity record costs graph metadata plus a file stat for SCIP-indexed symbols — no file read. Availability, path, and the definition range all come from the index, so record detail is O(metadata) for the overwhelming majority of entities.\n\nTHE EXCEPTION, and why it is unavoidable: a syntactic-fallback identity (`ts:` prefix) encodes path, language tag, and name — but NOT a range. Nothing but the file itself knows where that declaration currently sits, so `Substrate::definition_location` parses it, and `code_detail` pays that on the record detail route. Two properties keep it bounded rather than a lurking amplifier: the parse refuses files over its own 4 MiB ceiling, and it is memoized by mtime, so repeat views of the same file are free. Record detail is a SINGLE-record route (`code_detail` has exactly one caller, `GET /api/v1/records/{uuid}`), so the parse never fans out across a listing.\n\nWHY NOT DEFER THE PARSE to the source endpoint to restore a clean metadata-only rule: availability would become optimistic. Today a `ts:` entity whose declaration has been deleted resolves to no definition, and the record page says so from metadata alone. Deferring would advertise `source_available: true` and then fail with a 503 when the source route could not find the declaration either — trading a truthful answer for a late error. The cost guarantee is worth less than the honesty." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ae8fa7b-350f-4f7c-9840-0f32dee8257a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ae8fa7b-350f-4f7c-9840-0f32dee8257a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/ad2b7acf-fc5c-40b7-956d-aedd05b0cf96> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Consequence/8ae8fa7b-350f-4f7c-9840-0f32dee8257a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-17T05:27:04.569768Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
