<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c6e01ff-57cf-4867-bdbe-cdc74d39aa3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/86e20993-2092-4929-9acc-96c4f3efe9bb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c6e01ff-57cf-4867-bdbe-cdc74d39aa3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/e357f15c-b96a-4869-b6fe-733d6528f022> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c6e01ff-57cf-4867-bdbe-cdc74d39aa3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c6e01ff-57cf-4867-bdbe-cdc74d39aa3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/8d48edbd-7ee2-4a52-9eac-f2a09c858637> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c6e01ff-57cf-4867-bdbe-cdc74d39aa3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c6e01ff-57cf-4867-bdbe-cdc74d39aa3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Hard rule for every source-serving surface: repository text may be shown beside a CodeEntity record ONLY when the substrate can prove the on-disk FILE is the content it was indexed from, the resolved path stays inside the repository, and the request addresses this machine by address rather than by DNS name.\n\nTRUST — THE UNIT OF PROOF IS THE FILE, NOT `HEAD`. Bytes are admitted only through the generation-proven read (`indexed_started_at` plus a stable stat/read/stat). An edited working tree or an unverifiable baseline yields metadata plus a reindex explanation and NO preview. A moved `HEAD` whose file is provably unchanged IS served, flagged `substrate_stale`: its line numbers are still true, and withholding would blind the workbench whenever any unrelated file changed. Story code-anchor line numbers are published on the same terms, and travel with the path they were resolved in. Degrading to a warning is correct; degrading to approximately-right source is not.\n\nLOCATION. Definitions come from one substrate helper covering SCIP and the tree-sitter fallback; no surface locates a definition by searching a file for its name. Where a normalized symbol collides, the helper must choose the definition MINTING keeps — scope first, then lowest (file, symbol) — or a minted entity resolves to the definition minting dropped.\n\nCONTAINMENT. Checked after canonicalization, not by rejecting `..`: an indexed path can itself be a symlink, or sit under one, and reads follow symlinks. Only paths resolving inside the repository root are servable.\n\nBOUNDS. context = definition plus 12 surrounding lines, capped at 400 lines / 256 KiB; full = the whole indexed file, capped at 20,000 lines / 1 MiB, with a hard 8 MiB read ceiling above them. Availability is decided from file METADATA alone, so describing a record costs no read. Peak allocation is bounded by the window, never the file. A definition that does not fit inside the returned text is refused rather than advertised. Public positions are 1-based UTF-8 byte coordinates; clipping respects UTF-8 boundaries.\n\nORIGIN. The daemon's CORS layer is permissive by design for the knowledge API, but source text is the one payload where that is a real exposure. Comparing `Origin` to `Host` is NOT sufficient: both are caller-controlled, and a page whose DNS is rebound to loopback sends matching attacker-chosen values — and because that fetch is same-origin to the browser, it carries no `Origin` at all. A present `Host` must therefore be `localhost` or an address literal in every case; a DNS name is refused. Requests with no `Host` are not browser requests and are served. Source is rendered as escaped plain text — never as markup.\n\nSCOPE. This constrains presentation and reads only. Source locations are runtime substrate projections and are never persisted into the project knowledge graph." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/0c6e01ff-57cf-4867-bdbe-cdc74d39aa3b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
