<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/86e20993-2092-4929-9acc-96c4f3efe9bb> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/e357f15c-b96a-4869-b6fe-733d6528f022> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#constrains> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/8d48edbd-7ee2-4a52-9eac-f2a09c858637> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Hard rule for every source-serving surface: repository text may be shown beside a CodeEntity record ONLY when the substrate can prove the on-disk file is the same content it was indexed from, and the browser-facing route must refuse cross-origin reads.\n\nTRUST. Definition locations are resolved through one substrate helper covering both SCIP and the tree-sitter fallback. No surface may locate a definition by searching the file for its name — a lexical guess presented as a semantic location is the failure mode AD ec521d7d already forbids for LSP coordinates, and it is the same failure here. Source bytes are admitted only through the generation-proven read (Substrate::read_indexed_source: indexed_started_at plus a stable stat/read/stat), so a stale index, an edited working tree, an unverifiable baseline, or a path escaping the repo yields metadata plus a reindex explanation and NO preview. Degrading to a warning is correct; degrading to approximately-right source is not.\n\nBOUNDS. context = definition plus 12 surrounding lines, capped at 400 lines / 256 KiB; full = the whole indexed file, capped at 20,000 lines / 1 MiB. Public positions are 1-based UTF-8 byte coordinates, and clipping respects UTF-8 boundaries.\n\nORIGIN. The daemon's CORS layer is permissive by design for the knowledge API, but source text is the one payload where that is a real exposure: any page a developer visits could otherwise read their working tree from localhost. The source route therefore rejects a request carrying a cross-origin Origin header while allowing same-origin WebUI requests and local non-browser callers (no Origin). Source is rendered as escaped plain text — never as markup.\n\nSCOPE. This constrains presentation and reads only. Source locations are runtime substrate projections and are never persisted into the project knowledge graph." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Constraint/ecf8f7f0-b93e-404b-b075-dc1c57c23c93> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-16T02:05:04.647108Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
