<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/47f3f038-8fd7-4a96-9c74-15a24bf8be17> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/df808a17-3593-4c1b-9f12-5c28051cc931> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b824b26-36bb-47ce-a235-0a4fdf31a662> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A verification verdict needs a sentinel: exit code AND run-completed proof" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a verification run is only evidence once you can see BOTH that it finished and what status it finished with. Anything else — a filtered exit code, a partially-written log — reads exactly like success.\n\nTHE SHAPE THAT WORKS. Redirect the whole run to a file and append an explicit sentinel carrying the real status, then refuse to draw any conclusion until the sentinel is present:\n\n  cargo test --no-fail-fast > /tmp/suite.txt 2>&1; echo \"EXIT=$?\" >> /tmp/suite.txt\n  until grep -q EXIT= /tmp/suite.txt; do sleep 15; done\n\nThen read the sentinel, `test result:` lines, and the binary count together. `--no-fail-fast` matters: by default cargo stops at the first failing binary, so a truncated-looking log is ambiguous between \"still running\" and \"aborted on failure\".\n\nTWO WAYS THIS HAS FAILED, BOTH REPORTED AS GREEN.\n(1) FILTERED STATUS. `cargo test | tail -60` (2026-07-09) and `cargo test | grep -E ... > file; echo \"EXIT=$?\"` (2026-08-06) both exit 0 while cargo FAILED, because `$?` belongs to the LAST stage. The second was written after the first was recorded — the banned construct is any filter in the gating position, not the word `tail`.\n(2) MID-FLIGHT READ. On 2026-08-06 the results file was read while the run was in flight; 14 binaries had reported ok and the count was published as a green full suite. The run went on to fail 2 tests in `tests/mcp_replies.rs` — a real regression, found instead by an external code review. A log with no failures in it is not a log of a run with no failures.\n\nPROCESS COROLLARIES. Never treat `pgrep`-style liveness as the completion signal (it gave a false \"not running\" for a live cargo process in the same session); trust the sentinel you wrote. And when reporting, distinguish what was OBSERVED from what was INFERRED — \"312 tests, 0 failures\" asserted a total that had merely not failed *yet*.\n\nComplements Lesson 9a4470ef (scoped by default, full suite at acceptance gates — this governs how that gate is read) and Lesson 6fe1a3bd (verify the artifact, not the checkmark — the same distrust, one layer out)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/1e3faf61-58a9-416f-af61-4d9ff634847f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-07T00:03:07.380344Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "A verification verdict needs a sentinel: exit code AND run-completed proof" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/dff41e50-992c-4078-ac38-336884117cf5> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/06f53ce2-8df2-45c0-b0a0-892ab6089479> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e16bc762-1dc2-471e-9ad9-84716d029367> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e16bc762-1dc2-471e-9ad9-84716d029367> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tie cleanup to a value's lifetime, not to reaching the next line" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e16bc762-1dc2-471e-9ad9-84716d029367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e16bc762-1dc2-471e-9ad9-84716d029367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e16bc762-1dc2-471e-9ad9-84716d029367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: when a task publishes a result others are waiting on, the publish must be tied to the LIFETIME of the value that owns the claim (a drop guard), never to the task reaching the line that publishes. Any await between claiming and publishing is a point where the task can be cancelled and simply cease to exist, leaving the claim standing and the waiters parked forever.\n\nEVIDENCE (2026-08-17). Story narration coalesces concurrent requests: the first caller becomes the leader, inserts a flight into the cache, calls the provider, and records the result; later callers await a `tokio::sync::Notify`. An HTTP client that disconnects mid-narration cancels the handler future, so the leader vanished between starting the provider call and recording anything. The flight stayed in the map holding `None`, and every later request for that subject coalesced onto a flight nobody was driving — a permanent, subject-specific hang that survived until the daemon restarted, and that logged nothing at all. The 60s provider timeout never fired because no task was left to time out. Symptom was \"LLM narration hangs forever, but only for some subjects\"; the fix was `FlightLease` with a `Drop` that publishes an abandoned failure and removes the entry, so followers fall back to the symbolic article and the next caller genuinely retries.\n\nRULE. Any claim registered in shared state before an await must be released by a guard type, not by control flow. Same shape as Lesson bdb02873 (prove the file between stat and read) in a concurrency setting: correctness cannot depend on the happy path being reached. Test it by dropping the leader mid-flight and asserting the follower resolves — `an_abandoned_leader_does_not_strand_its_followers` in src/stories/narration/cache.rs.\n\nDIAGNOSTIC NOTE: silent abandonment was the main obstacle. A guard that fires on the sad path should say so at debug level, or the next occurrence is diagnosed from CPU idleness and parked worker threads again." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e16bc762-1dc2-471e-9ad9-84716d029367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e16bc762-1dc2-471e-9ad9-84716d029367> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-19T04:42:46.596006Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
