<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "codex exec hangs on piped stdin" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "mcp" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "codex exec (codex-cli 0.141.0) reads ADDITIONAL instructions from stdin when stdin is a PIPE rather than a TTY, and blocks until EOF (help: 'If stdin is piped and a prompt is also provided, stdin is appended as a <stdin> block'). bench/run.py used subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True) with NO stdin=, so the codex child inherited an open pipe under non-interactive launch (agent/cron) and HUNG the full CELL_TIMEOUT (600s) producing 0 tokens, 0 events, no MCP tool call (the raw events.json was 0 bytes). MASKED when the bench scripts are launched via the user's interactive `!` TTY (the scripts even say 'Launch via `!`'); the bug surfaces ONLY under automation. ROOT-CAUSE FIX: stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL on the agent subprocess in run.py (the prompt is always passed as an arg, so the agent never needs stdin). Minimal repro/verification: `codex exec -m gpt-5.4-mini --json 'reply OK' < /dev/null` exits in ~6s with output, vs hanging indefinitely without the redirect. Extends the harness-pitfalls Lesson 5ac2174a (which covered opencode/LM Studio); this is the codex-backend analogue." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T09:14:00.327731Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e1e4091c-0a8e-4445-ad6d-521be2644c60> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Benchmark harness pitfall: `codex exec` reads piped stdin and blocks on EOF — an unattended/agent launch (no TTY) hangs the full cell timeout with zero output; fix stdin=DEVNULL" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Freeze trial instruments, not product versions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Longitudinal trial validity requires frozen probes, primary-source gold answers, judge/rubric, month-0 baseline, and kill thresholds; it does not require holding MOOSEDev to an obsolete implementation. Continue improving the product, and stamp every raw and judged row with a trial epoch derived from the running health version plus binary SHA-256. Pair B0/B2 only within an epoch and report mixed epochs separately, while preserving the original longitudinal baseline and thresholds across epoch boundaries. This exposes software evolution as a measured dimension instead of either hiding it or resetting the trial whenever MOOSEDev improves." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T00:42:10.705451Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Freeze trial instruments, not product versions" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e209a0d9-e218-4bcd-b531-607b6a2ecf04> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07415633-e7f0-410b-9eec-2a7bf9fcff97> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Local-first project memory is Git-shared, not machine-local" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: describing MOOSEDev as local or per-project can be misread as saying its knowledge is private to one machine or one user. The live RocksDB store is local and derived, but `.moosedev/kg.nq` is the canonical project graph, exported automatically, checked into the repository, reviewed and merged with code, and used to hydrate other clones. Rule: when comparing MOOSEDev with centralized organizational-memory products, say that MOOSEDev shares durable project knowledge asynchronously through Git; reserve the contrast for centralized real-time organization scope, connectors, and access control—not shared versus unshared memory." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-20T21:48:07.722564Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Local-first project memory is Git-shared, not machine-local" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e38bb6a1-c4a9-449c-b6a7-e306e117fe0a> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/013a9706-3932-4ce5-8777-64aab321cc32> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Phase-2 turf (corrected): B2 ties mem0 on relevance + currency, wins completeness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "CORRECTED Phase-2 codegraph competitor result (supersedes 8120780a, which was confounded by the dead-MCP bug, Lesson 0a890ea9).\n\nRELEVANCE (mem0's turf) — TIE. With a WORKING MCP, B2 (gpt-5.4-mini) calls get_relevant_context 4/4 at ~35k tokens, cov ~0.82; mem0's recall ~40k tokens, cov 0.67-0.90 — comparable cost AND accuracy. Oracle/push cheaper (~16k). The earlier \"B2 thrashes / mem0 wins relevance\" was ENTIRELY a broken MOOSEDEV_BIN -> dead MCP -> grep fallback (0.5-1.2M tokens), NOT a model/prompt/capability problem (the weak-model and store-grep-instinct hypotheses were both refuted by the fix). CAVEAT: relevance markers are prior-contaminated (cold B0 0.33-0.80), so coverage is noisy; the tool-usage + token parity is the robust tie signal.\n\nCURRENCY (mem0's temporal turf) — TIE. All memory arms 1.00 on the cur_mcp_handshake reversal; cold B0 0.00 (stale).\n\nCOMPLETENESS / NEGATION / SUPERSESSION (B2's turf) — B2 CATEGORICAL, fair + judge-validated: B2 1.00 vs mem0 ~0.15 vs notes ~0.05. UNAFFECTED by the bug (the complete set is recoverable from B2's structured store regardless of query mechanism; mem0's top-k cannot enumerate it by any means).\n\nSYNTHESIS (clean): MOOSEDev TIES mem0 where mem0 is built to win (simple relevance recall + currency) and WINS categorically on completeness/negation/traversal — a SUPERSET on the structural axis, parity on mem0's. The inverse-trades intuition (mem0 cheap-but-incomplete) holds in spirit, but mem0 does NOT beat B2 on relevance; they tie. Relates to Lessons 0a890ea9 (the bug), a6529240 (judge fairness), 243c6c89/8a06ad1d (capability axis). Full matrix: bench/EVALUATION_MEM0.md." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasRationale> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Rationale/29297125-b214-4e7d-99ee-beb938c15e98> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T19:03:27.891068Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Phase-2 turf (corrected): B2 ties mem0 on relevance + currency, wins completeness" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e80db883-7235-4283-aef2-34eddc4b961c> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#supersedes> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/8120780a-7042-46e1-be18-5662977baacd> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reader copy must hide Story implementation vocabulary" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/8d48edbd-7ee2-4a52-9eac-f2a09c858637> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Provenance text can be technically accurate and still harm comprehension when it exposes internal terms such as beat prose, route, or graph projection. Prevention rule: keep implementation vocabulary in code and specifications; reader-facing status text should describe what the person sees and what MOOSEDev guarantees in ordinary language, while still identifying LLM-written explanation and deterministic evidence selection." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-15T01:00:32.272835Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Reader copy must hide Story implementation vocabulary" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/e9e75b73-3161-4c21-ac6c-5a0cc2328d89> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/33d9ad51-8ed9-4fbd-a76c-69d9d09e3157> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Config discovery gated on a build artifact silently excluded non-Rust adopters" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a documented configuration mechanism was gated on `Cargo.toml`, so it silently did nothing for every adopter whose project is not the shape we develop in — and the defect was invisible because the fallback path looked like success.\n\nWHAT HAPPENED. AD 510c5585 established the repo-root `.env` (dotenv fills only unset vars; explicit env wins). The implementation walked ancestors of cwd and `current_exe`, accepting a directory as the repo root ONLY if it contained `Cargo.toml`, and put the compile-time `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` first in the candidate list with a break-on-first-hit. Two consequences: (1) a Python or TypeScript project — both first-class targets, detected by the substrate producers via pyproject.toml / setup.py / requirements.txt / package.json — never had its `.env` read at all, though README and `--help` both promise \"repo-root .env\"; (2) a dev build always preferred MOOSEDev's own `.env` over the project the user was actually in.\n\nWHY IT SURVIVED. `repo_dotenv_candidates` had no test — the only dotenv coverage exercised `load_dotenv_file` (precedence), not discovery. And the failure is silent-and-plausible: with no `.env` found, the data dir falls back to the `.moosedev` default and a store is created successfully, so the CLI attaches to a stray cwd-relative store instead of erroring. Reproduced 2026-08-04 on the shipped binary: in a `pyproject.toml` fixture whose `.env` set a custom MOOSEDEV_DATA_DIR, v0.7.0 created `.moosedev/` and ignored the setting; the fix created the configured dir and no stray.\n\nTHE RULE. Before shipping a configuration path, verify it on a repo shape you do NOT build in. Language-agnostic tools acquire language-specific assumptions through exactly this route: a marker chosen because it was the marker at hand. Corollary: when a config lookup can fail into a working default, it needs a test at the discovery layer, because no user-visible error will ever report it.\n\nRESOLUTION (0.7.1). Root markers are `.git` plus the manifests of every supported language; the walk runs cwd-upward nearest-first, stops at the first root so it can never reach $HOME, and CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR moves last as a dev-build fallback. Deliberately NOT shared with the producers' language detection, which answers a stricter and different question (TypeScript demands tsconfig.json AND package.json before spawning an indexer)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-06T03:27:52.086276Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Config discovery gated on a build artifact silently excluded non-Rust adopters" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/510c5585-6ff1-4ff1-abff-a7467adc5b71> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea1faf22-1260-4196-b64d-4706d8aea695> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/e43baa99-7ced-4e24-a526-f5aa9cb2235b> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not infer systematic LSP drift from sparse squiggle locations" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: squiggles appearing on wrong editor lines do not by themselves prove a saved-file versus active-buffer offset. The exact-line-alignment change was based on that inference, but the user's follow-up observation showed the remaining locations are seemingly random. Rule: before changing position mapping, capture the emitted publishDiagnostics payload and compare each diagnostic's source entity, server range, active-buffer range, and rendered Zed line; require a repeatable transformation before selecting a mapping fix." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-17T04:09:16.711518Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Do not infer systematic LSP drift from sparse squiggle locations" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ea6c568d-ef9b-4c43-b091-8bf24ef28a86> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/fd89fa33-0a65-49de-8d34-105b0ab9a7ea> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bound Story narration to the provider's real budget" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: Story narration became unreliable when a local model was given several large concurrent JSON-producing calls with fixed per-stage timeouts. Measured LM Studio traces showed repeated 12-second client disconnects, truncated JSON, and intermittent final schema failures; JSON repair cannot recover missing completions or structurally wrong objects. Prevention rule: treat the configured model context window as a hard upper bound, reserve room for output and protocol overhead, build one deterministic bounded evidence packet for the default path, prefer one structured synthesis call with short server-expanded source IDs, cache successful narration by projection fingerprint, and emit stage-level timing and validation diagnostics without logging evidence or model output." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-15T06:06:09.146367Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Bound Story narration to the provider's real budget" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/53720fee-d7ff-43d3-943f-64acff2fe112> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eb189914-17c0-45f3-837e-c530b7e58958> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d1e04b46-ff2e-419d-be2f-7f0e4cb6a76d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Persist workflow-required inverse edges at mutation time" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/402e5c0b-dc22-4063-84c6-6b9dd954d540> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Persist workflow-required inverse edges at mutation time. An owl:inverseOf declaration does not guarantee that a consumer will observe the reverse edge: enrichment can be lazy, unavailable, bypassed by a reader, or hidden behind a stale derived cache. When a lifecycle view traverses the reverse direction as an integrity-critical part of the workflow, the mutation must atomically assert both the canonical edge and its inverse; reasoning remains optional derived enrichment, not a correctness precondition. Regression rule: verify both directions immediately after the write, before calling enrichment. This prevents a superseded record from losing its visible successor." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-15T01:33:03.97554Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/eec7ac12-6551-4de8-92c8-ff4a3c216d5d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Persist workflow-required inverse edges at mutation time" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fragmented evidence cards do not restore a mental model" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/811afb5c-3fb5-4b7d-b861-b9e68de8e2c8> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/8d48edbd-7ee2-4a52-9eac-f2a09c858637> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: dividing a comprehension aid into separately generated evidence cards can preserve grounding while still failing its human purpose. The first live Story experience produced terse, jargon-heavy blocks that did not connect causes, decisions, code, risks, or change over time. Prevention rule: assemble the complete typed subject dossier first, organize it causally and chronologically, and render one cohesive account; keep citations, timeline, and gaps inspectable outside the prose rather than making UI containers define the explanation." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-15T02:09:44.591548Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Fragmented evidence cards do not restore a mental model" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f0c35d76-67ef-472e-a74b-d44f084b37f9> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/d1e04b46-ff2e-419d-be2f-7f0e4cb6a76d> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Direct store writes leave the dense index stale" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/3193c9a7-8f50-4af0-b0b6-f05ebaa23393> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "mcp" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "A direct oxigraph write to the project store (bulk migration / label surgery) bypasses graph::index_record, so the durable instance dense index (instance-vectors.db) does NOT reflect the change: build_instance_index's incremental check is by-IRI (record already has a vector -> '0 to embed'), not by-content-hash, even though record_embed_text = rdfs:label + hasDescription. BM25F is unaffected because EntityIndexCache rebuilds from the store on serve restart. Fix: force a dense refresh — delete instance-vectors.db and restart for a cold rebuild (logged 'embedded 137/137'), or re-call index_record per changed IRI. Surfaced relabeling 121 content-shaped rdfs:labels to short designator handles on the dogfood store (the MOOSE label-designator contract): rdfs:label -> short NAME (0 over 80c, max 77, avg 52), hasTitle kept the full original title (max 359c) so the migration is lossless and 'hasTitle duplicates rdfs:label' no longer holds but nothing reads hasTitle for retrieval. 0 SHACL violations after. See examples/relabel_apply.rs + examples/audit_labels.rs." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T19:09:26.064336Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f1f86296-8bdb-449f-81f2-eef4cdef2d8e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Direct store writes leave the dense index stale" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dev-only friction is not a product gap" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "During slice-3 Zed acceptance, the extension's PATH lookup found the installed 0.6.3 release (no lsp subcommand) instead of the dev build - and the fix was a one-line project-local settings override. Proposed product changes (auto-writing binary overrides in init, version-checking in the extension) were scoped out by James: only developers working on moosedev itself ever run a dev build beside an installed release; users get binaries where PATH resolution just works. Rule: before proposing a fix, ask who actually hits the problem - friction confined to the project's own developers gets a README line or a settings snippet, not product surface." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-10T00:32:22.601586Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Dev-only friction is not a product gap" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f20d266b-0983-4f66-8daf-2e7a5598018e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/a7fc1353-2b7a-42c9-ab64-bd0043e412f6> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Month-1 checkpoint: trivyn gap widened, moose null, guard false-flags" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Month-1 in-anger checkpoint (2026-07-24; gpt-5.4-mini agent, local-qat blind judge, first fingerprinted epoch 0.7.0+721698cf0251 — month-0 rows report as legacy-unversioned): trivyn mean gap judge(B2)−judge(B0) = +0.40 (n=10) vs +0.10 at month-0 — the predicted widening: B0 decayed on editions_sqlite_pg_split and moose_only_alignment (1→0) while B2 held, and BOTH month-0 B2 losers (yasqe, editions) recovered to 1.0. moose = 0.00 (n=6) vs +0.25 — an honest NULL: cold B0 recovered role_routed_arctic_fleet and shape_aware_filter_resolution and scored 1.0 everywhere (rationale locally recoverable at current HEAD, or judge/agent noise; reported, not spun). Engagement (PRIMARY kill guard, Constraint 75b0cf14): trivyn fires=23 misses=9, moose fires=98 misses=57 — both far above the ≥4/project/month threshold; SECONDARY needs ≥3 months. moose's 57 misses are a capture-gap signal worth triage.\n\nOPERATIONAL LESSONS: (1) The dead-MCP guard is too narrow — it counts only get_relevant_context, so 4 of 16 B2 cells were flagged \"datum suspect\" while demonstrably alive via query/sparql calls (one moose agent even read the store's kg.nq bytes with shell strings/sed — graph-derived, just outside the MCP surface). Proof-of-life should be ANY successful moosedev tool call; false flags erode trust in the void rule (Lesson 0a890ea9). (2) Harness-owned serves must pin MOOSEDEV_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1:0 — the moosedev repo's .env (127.0.0.1:7474, the dogfood workbench) leaks into spawned daemons via the dotenv ancestor-walk; the port collision silently suppressed http.addr publication, which broke the trial-epoch fingerprint (Lesson 3ea68212's identity check correctly refused to run). dotenvy fills only unset vars, so the explicit env pin wins; fixed in bench/run_trial_month.sh 2026-07-24. Project daemons are unaffected (trivyn pins 7475, moose 7476 via their .mcp.json)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-24T15:50:53.594829Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Month-1 checkpoint: trivyn gap widened, moose null, guard false-flags" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#isSupersededBy> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/2f00e722-cfe7-4ec0-84d3-bca29cadfc71> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f223ba6b-a21a-4416-ac3a-37c0dd043c1f> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/07415633-e7f0-410b-9eec-2a7bf9fcff97> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Valid memory task: not default, not recoverable" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/402e5c0b-dc22-4063-84c6-6b9dd954d540> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Refines Lesson a80bbe88. A task measures memory's value only if its correct action (a) is NOT the model's default and (b) is NOT recoverable from the working code OR git history. On a clean codebase almost all code rules fail (b) — frontier models trace them (see the frontier-traces-code lesson). Truly memory_only knowledge is why/why-not RATIONALE for a DELETED approach (e.g. trivyn's \"the old data-to-TLO merge was abandoned because reconciling two ontologies through the shared top-level ontology is too coarse a join key — two unrelated classes both landing on a generic TLO class says nothing about sameness\"): the rejected code is gone, so it cannot be traced from the working tree. BUT the git-history check is decisive and was run: the WHY is absent from ALL 537 commit MESSAGES (zero hits for coarse / \"join key\" / granularity / equivalentClass), yet it IS in the committed design doc spec/referenceable-ontologies.md — and trivyn's records were bootstrapped from that doc. So a frontier model with the FULL repo + git history can in principle recover it (git-show the doc). Therefore, for a well-documented repo, memory's frontier edge is EFFICIENCY (one query vs mining 537 commits / 90 doc files) + RELIABILITY (knowing to look) + CURRENCY (supersession-aware) + DELIVERY (push to local models that won't mine), NOT unique knowledge. Memory's unique-knowledge value appears only when docs/history are absent, stale, or lost — the comprehension-debt condition the benchmark simulates by stripping docs from the agent's working tree." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T02:49:46.104873Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f2f4cd99-127f-45f5-9e02-b203351daa24> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Valid memory-task design: correct action must be neither the model's default nor recoverable from code/git-history; vs a frontier model with full history, memory's edge is efficiency/currency/delivery, not unique knowledge" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "B1 export dropped SystemComponents via hasTitle assumption" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The bench B1 pipeline (export_corpus.py, parity_check.py) enumerated records via hasTitle. Fix B / AD 73918962 (label-property decoupling) made SystemComponents carry their label in hasComponentName, not hasTitle, so the export SILENTLY dropped all 8 SystemComponents (34 of 42 burrow records) and parity reported a mismatch. Separately, the chunk text now bakes in '# title' + a 'Lifecycle status:' line, so parity_check's exact body==hasDescription comparison failed for every chunk. FIXES: (1) export_corpus.py enumerates by rdfs:label — the canonical label EVERY record carries (including SystemComponents), the same field get_relevant_context searches; rdfs:label is a W3C standard (not the volatile ontology namespace), so binding to it is consistent with decouple-code-from-ontology-ttl. (2) parity_check.py checks the description is CONTAINED in the (intentionally richer) chunk text rather than byte-equal. GENERALIZED (extends Lesson 51b09e67): when a write-path is made label-property-agnostic (it writes each class's declared labelProperty), audit DOWNSTREAM CONSUMERS that hardcoded a fixed label property — they will silently under-select without erroring. For record enumeration, depend on the stable canonical label (rdfs:label), not a class-specific typed property." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T19:27:44.480336Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "B1 export silently dropped SystemComponents (hasTitle assumption) after the label-property decoupling; enumerate records by rdfs:label, the canonical label" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f30307ee-356c-4877-98f1-f64a92988b27> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/73918962-4171-4a97-b666-ae51f7958f80> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f36482eb-4fff-4049-ac81-8aa528033edc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f36482eb-4fff-4049-ac81-8aa528033edc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Capture surface creates no inter-record edges except supersession" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f36482eb-4fff-4049-ac81-8aa528033edc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f36482eb-4fff-4049-ac81-8aa528033edc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Proven against the dogfood (moosedev-on-itself) project graph via sparql: the ONLY record→record edges in the whole graph are `supersedes` (×8) and `hasRationale` (×10) — both created exclusively by supersede_decision — plus prov:* provenance. There is NO relatesTo / refines / dependsOn / extends edge of any kind. Notably, this session's dogfood records contain many [[wikilinks]] in their description TEXT, and none were materialized into edges — MOOSEDev does not resolve [[ ]] (it is a .claude auto-memory convention, not a graph mechanism). Capture-surface facts: record_important_decision accepts only title/kind/description/status (no relationship param); align_concepts/suggest_mappings link to the ONTOLOGY/vocab, not between records; supersede_decision is the sole inter-record semantic-edge primitive. CONCLUSION: this — not the bootstrap skill — is the root cause of the flat trivyn corpus (Lesson 0b2a0f80) and the structured≈free-text null (679a69af, fa9170f6). The bootstrap correctly captured high-signal typed records; it could not link them because no linking primitive exists, so MOOSEDev's 'living knowledge GRAPH' is presently a typed LIST + supersession chains, and the traversal/related-context portion of the structured value proposition is unbuilt. Scope note: zero supersessions at bootstrap is partly expected (point-in-time snapshot, nothing to supersede); and the bootstrap flattened at least one real evolution (the data-to-TLO merge abandonment) into a descriptive Lesson rather than a supersedes chain. IMPLICATION for the structured-memory thesis and for benchmark task design: supersession is the ONLY structural mechanism MOOSEDev can express today, so the currency/H4 'structural kill-shot' is not merely the cleanest structured-vs-free-text test — it is the only one the current product can support. Open design decision (candidate Requirement): give MOOSEDev a first-class record-relationship primitive (and/or materialize [[ ]]) so capture and bootstrap produce an actual relational graph." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f36482eb-4fff-4049-ac81-8aa528033edc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f36482eb-4fff-4049-ac81-8aa528033edc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T06:55:24.044356Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f36482eb-4fff-4049-ac81-8aa528033edc> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "MOOSEDev's capture surface creates NO inter-record relationship except supersession — so capture/bootstrap yield a typed LIST + supersession chains, not a relational graph (root cause of the flat-corpus finding)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Save-suppression keyed on a lagging baseline strands the index" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code-recovery" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: a server-side heuristic suppressed didSave reindex nudges when the saved text was byte-identical to the session's base_text ('unchanged, so positions cannot have shifted'). base_text is an ASYNC-LAGGING mirror of the indexed generation: it re-bases only on the session's 2s tick after a rebuild publishes. Observed live 2026-07-17: edit-save -> rebuild published; a fast revert-save landed before the tick, matched the STALE base_text, was suppressed, and the index stayed stranded at the pre-revert tree with no future nudge coming (the scripted revert cycle failed deterministically; unit and integration tests all passed because none reproduced the publish-then-save-within-2s timing). Rule: a heuristic that suppresses reconciliation must be keyed on state that provably matches the reconciled artifact, never on an asynchronously-updated mirror of it; when the cheap guard cannot prove equivalence, always schedule reconciliation and let the debounce absorb the cost. Corollary: push-surface liveness features need a live adversarial-timing check (fast undo, save during reload) on the real daemon before acceptance - the suite's green run missed exactly the window the tick granularity creates." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-07-17T15:28:48.772987Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Save-suppression keyed on a lagging baseline strands the index" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f3a78f90-5b4d-46b6-9539-357d82b365ee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/5dfe9a84-38fa-4a66-8e00-e715e0309e90> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f84b4b21-3097-41ff-82b0-dcf609564ec0> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f84b4b21-3097-41ff-82b0-dcf609564ec0> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Distinguish canonical RDF export from convenience output" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f84b4b21-3097-41ff-82b0-dcf609564ec0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f84b4b21-3097-41ff-82b0-dcf609564ec0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "User review correction from the graph-export implementation: do not describe every RDF export format as equally deterministic or version-control safe. N-Quads is the canonical dataset export because it preserves named graph identity and sorted quads are byte-stable. N-Triples can be deterministic only after graph names are deliberately dropped. Turtle is human-readable and serializer-shaped, not byte-canonical. When exporting multiple named graphs to graph-only formats such as N-Triples or Turtle, strip graph names intentionally and deduplicate by subject/predicate/object so the output is a true triple union rather than duplicated triples from each named graph. CLI export should also reject a missing store instead of letting Store::open create an empty one that misleadingly dumps 0 quads, and file-writing tool docs should recommend absolute paths for MCP clients." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f84b4b21-3097-41ff-82b0-dcf609564ec0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f84b4b21-3097-41ff-82b0-dcf609564ec0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-20T18:47:38.592194Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f84b4b21-3097-41ff-82b0-dcf609564ec0> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "RDF export surfaces must distinguish canonical dataset export from graph-format convenience output" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MOOSEDev read cost is query-dependent: the 1.68M set-completeness run was an agent dump, not tool overhead" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "CORRECTION (user-driven) to the \"MOOSEDev efficiency downside\" framing. The codegraph B2 set_all_constraints run cost 1.68M agent tokens NOT because completeness is inherently expensive in MOOSEDev, but because the AGENT dumped records via list_mcp_resources (tools=['list_mcp_resources','list_mcp_resources']) instead of issuing a targeted SPARQL. The exact complete set returns in ~hundreds of tokens via ONE clean query (Lesson 392855d0: B2 tool-ceiling = exact SPARQL set, ~hundreds of tokens).\n\nTHE MODEL: MOOSEDev's READ COST IS QUERY-DEPENDENT — a DIAL, not a fixed overhead. (a) Targeted relevance via get_relevant_context is as cheap AND as easy as mem0's recall(query) — same skill floor, parity tokens. (b) Completeness/structure via SPARQL is cheap IF queried well, and is a capability mem0 lacks entirely. So MOOSEDev is a SUPERSET of mem0's read behavior, not a costlier alternative.\n\nTHE REAL DEPENDENCY (what actually gets robbed): AGENT QUERY COMPETENCE — \"depends how the coding agent uses it.\" A poorly-driving agent OVER-fetches (the 1.68M list_mcp_resources dump) or UNDER-queries (misses the structured advantage). mem0's genuine edge here is its TRIVIAL SKILL FLOOR (recall needs no query authoring, hard to misuse); MOOSEDev matches it for the targeted case (get_relevant_context) but the SPARQL power tier needs competence.\n\nTHE COVER (design intent, not yet measured): the active/push layer (AD 145af7e9; push plugin AD 03393c63) is meant to drive the RIGHT query, and the v3 symbolic-controller vision (Requirement 350c7f2e) puts the symbolic layer — not the LLM — in charge of querying, so the payoff stops hinging on the LLM authoring SPARQL well (\"LLM as sensor, symbolic layer as controller\", invariant #1).\n\nHOW TO APPLY: never report a high B2 read-token figure as MOOSEDev's inherent efficiency cost — attribute it to agent query STRATEGY and report the targeted-query cost alongside. For competitor token comparisons, compare like-for-like (targeted vs targeted); price completeness separately (only MOOSEDev can deliver it). Refines the EVALUATION_MEM0.md efficiency note; relates to Lessons 392855d0 (tool ceiling), 8a06ad1d (capability axis), a6529240 (grading fairness)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-23T17:14:33.356187Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "MOOSEDev read cost is query-dependent: the 1.68M set-completeness run was an agent dump, not tool overhead" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/145af7e9-c8ad-40e1-91ab-e4442d861733> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/47f3f038-8fd7-4a96-9c74-15a24bf8be17> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/f8f2f87c-4b2a-436c-abfb-23cf32e08cc3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/7b824b26-36bb-47ce-a235-0a4fdf31a662> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fa9170f6-ac97-4264-9c66-77eecf55e47d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fa9170f6-ac97-4264-9c66-77eecf55e47d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Q&A efficiency matrix: local push dominates" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fa9170f6-ac97-4264-9c66-77eecf55e47d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fa9170f6-ac97-4264-9c66-77eecf55e47d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "First clean delivery-vs-cost result on a comprehension-debt Q&A task (rationale doc stripped from the agent tree, no git history). Task: explain why the data-to-TLO ontology merge was rejected. Two models × conditions, N=3 trials, means. LOCAL A3B (qwen3.6-35b-a3b-mlx): cold 0.12 score / 681,987 prompt-tok / 24.3 tool-calls / 257s; pull (B2 tooluse) 0.00 / 820,174 / 24.0 / 375s; push (B2 oracle) 0.90 / 9,798 / 0.0 / 35s. → Push DOMINATES every axis (70× fewer prompt tokens than cold, 0 vs 24 tools, 1 vs 19 steps, 7× faster) AND is the only condition that answers correctly. Pull is ACTIVELY HARMFUL for local: 0/3 correct (worse than cold) and the MOST expensive — when the A3B engages the memory tools it thrashes harder (one trial 2.34M tokens / 61 tool-calls incl. 30 bash + get_relevant_context+query+sparql, still 0.0; one timed out at 600s). Handing a local model memory tools just adds ways to flail; the symbolic layer must retrieve (invariant #1). FRONTIER gpt-5.5: cold 0.70 / 49,616 / 22.3 / 67s; b1-md (ambient markdown in tree) 0.70 / 19,518 / 2.3; b1-rag (free-text recall tool) 0.90 / 7,882 / 1.0; pull (structured tool) 0.58 / 20,006 / 3.0; push 0.70 / 6,027 / 0.0 / 7s. → Frontier recovers the 'why' cold by exploration (0.70), so memory's frontier edge is EFFICIENCY not accuracy: at matched ~0.70 accuracy, push costs 8× fewer prompt tokens, 22→0 tool-calls, ~10× faster than cold. Frontier PULLS reliably (every pull/rag cell made its memory call), so the local push-only necessity does not apply — a single recall call (b1-rag) is the frontier sweet spot. TWO HONEST NULLS/CAVEATS: (1) structured (B2) did NOT beat free-text (B1) — free-text edged it (rag 0.90 ≥ push/pull 0.58-0.70) — the EXPECTED single-hop null (hop_count=1; one lookup suffices), reinforcing Lesson 679a69af; structured's edge needs a MULTI-HOP task, untested. (2) Scores are keyword-coverage-graded (paraphrase-penalizing): gpt-5.5 push 0.70 (rephrases) < A3B push 0.90 (parrots the record) is almost certainly a grading artifact, not worse frontier answers — so cross-model ACCURACY is noisy while the EFFICIENCY/THRASHING metrics are robust and comparable (LLM-judge is the fix, per the task spec). Net: token-efficiency + thrashing-reduction is the UNIVERSAL win (local 70×, frontier 8×; both 24→0 tools); accuracy is a big win for weak models (knowledge-gap closing) and a wash for frontier. Demonstrates Lesson f2f4cd99 (frontier edge = efficiency) with numbers; extends push AD 03393c63 and the local-pull Lesson 2dcca5ff (pull now shown HARMFUL, not merely ignored, for local)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fa9170f6-ac97-4264-9c66-77eecf55e47d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fa9170f6-ac97-4264-9c66-77eecf55e47d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-19T06:21:50.518133Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fa9170f6-ac97-4264-9c66-77eecf55e47d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Q&A efficiency matrix (whynot_tlo_merge, N=3): for LOCAL models push dominates and pull is actively harmful; for FRONTIER memory is an efficiency play, not an accuracy play; structured≈free-text on single-hop" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pin the agent temperature server-side in LM Studio" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/f4d2f589-8f00-4640-ae16-fbb0184cb365> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Benchmark setup finding. The agent-under-test runs via opencode, whose config exposes no temperature/top_p/seed (only timeout-type provider options and --variant for reasoning effort), so temperature must be pinned SERVER-SIDE in LM Studio (per-model default, reload to apply). MOOSEDev's internal NLQ client already sends temperature 0 (src/llm/mod.rs:116, unwrap_or(0.0)), so only the agent needed pinning. Verified empirically: before pinning, repeated B2 runs drifted (score 1.0 then 0.767); after setting qwen3.6-27b to temp 0 + reload, 3/3 repeats scored 1.0 with tightly clustered token counts — confirming LM Studio temp 0 is the effective control (opencode does not override it with its own temperature). IMPORTANT: temp 0 is NOT bit-exact determinism on local MoE inference — the three temp-0 outputs still differed in wording/length (different sha, len 584/609/498) due to Metal FP non-associativity, MoE expert routing, and batching. So temperature 0 collapses OUTCOME (score) variance but not token-exact output; keep N trials + mean±CI in the matrix for honest confidence intervals. Rule: set agent temperature 0 in LM Studio per model + reload; do not expect identical transcripts; report mean±CI over trials, not single runs. Relates to the 4-arm skeleton (Lesson 51f65b34)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T16:49:45.524159Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fcb8eb30-5c8e-49e8-bea7-ffcfcadda242> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Pin the agent temperature in LM Studio (opencode exposes no temperature config); temp 0 stabilizes the graded score but local-MoE inference keeps text-level non-determinism" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "One question about the graph deserves exactly one oracle" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/CodeEntity/e366550e-915a-4ba5-affe-a844d36c98d2> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/11e01ea2-f520-4f7c-a165-09532dacd43f> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Pattern: when a new surface needs to answer a question another surface already answers about the graph, find and call that oracle — do not write the predicate again, however small it looks. Two implementations of \"does the graph record anything about this entity?\" will diverge on lifecycle or predicate coverage long before anyone notices, and the divergence surfaces as the product contradicting itself.\n\nEVIDENCE (2026-08-18). The Story subject catalog grew its own rule for whether a CodeEntity has recorded knowledge: any typed edge to any record, any lifecycle status. `graph::dossier::direct_records_for_entity` already answered exactly that question through `LinkPairs` (the five ontology pairs, both directions) plus `is_dossier_visible` (working set or superseded), and src/graph/debt.rs says the reuse is deliberate — \"the metric counts exactly what a human sees on hover\". Within one day the two disagreed in the wild: entity `tests` (a1bdb0fc) had a single linking record, `a8f1e533`, status deprecated. Hover and the why-coverage metric hid it; the Story catalog advertised the entity as knowledge-bearing and would have generated a Story from a record the rest of the product treats as gone.\n\nRULE. Before writing a graph predicate, grep for the question, not the implementation (\"records for entity\", not \"quads_for_pattern\"). If the shared oracle genuinely does not fit at your scale, add a bulk form NEXT TO IT that reuses its predicate set and its lifecycle policy, rather than a private copy in the calling module. If you must differ from it deliberately, state the difference at the function — an undocumented divergence is indistinguishable from a bug and will be \"fixed\" in whichever direction the next reader guesses.\n\nBONUS: the shared form was also faster. One predicate-bound scan per pair replaced one subject scan per entity, taking the catalog endpoint from 262ms to 163ms." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-19T04:42:36.002564Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "One question about the graph deserves exactly one oracle" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/fe142c89-1b5c-4b4f-b81f-8c234718a534> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#learnedFrom> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/ArchitecturalDecision/6113c49b-f5c2-401e-9687-516a098ebfd5> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ffb79129-53d0-436e-9317-2cbb5703183d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Lesson> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ffb79129-53d0-436e-9317-2cbb5703183d> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dense index startup cost: cold vs warm" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ffb79129-53d0-436e-9317-2cbb5703183d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "mcp" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ffb79129-53d0-436e-9317-2cbb5703183d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Empirical startup cost of build_instance_index on the trivyn-temporal graph: COLD build embedded all 416 records in 107s (snowflake-arctic-embed-s, CPU); WARM restart on the persisted instance-vectors.db re-embedded 0 (serve log: '[instance-vectors] index warm (416 records, 0 to embed)') and the socket came up in seconds. Confirms the durable+incremental decision (b933bd10): without persistence every benchmark serve restart would re-pay the 107s cold build; with it, only the first boot pays and cost is proportional to churn, not graph size. Practical note for benches: pre-warm the index once before a matrix so the first cell is not skewed by the cold build." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ffb79129-53d0-436e-9317-2cbb5703183d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ffb79129-53d0-436e-9317-2cbb5703183d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-21T09:14:01.391968Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Lesson/ffb79129-53d0-436e-9317-2cbb5703183d> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Durable instance dense index startup cost: 107s cold build for 416 records (trivyn-temporal), 0 on warm restart — validates the durable+incremental decision" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/613cb623-9ee8-4eaa-80db-c1e8e83b40f3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/613cb623-9ee8-4eaa-80db-c1e8e83b40f3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Modernize a pre-GROWL store by re-serving, not re-bootstrapping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/613cb623-9ee8-4eaa-80db-c1e8e83b40f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/613cb623-9ee8-4eaa-80db-c1e8e83b40f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Re-serving a pre-GROWL store with the GROWL+new-core binary materializes inverse/subproperty edges into kg/project on the FIRST read (AppState bootstraps inferred_stale=true; ensure_enriched -> enrich_now persists, idempotent), with ZERO change to asserted records or supersede chains — so it is the cheap, safe way to bring a stale store current vs a from-scratch re-bootstrap. Verified 2026-06-22 on three bench stores: burrow 46->92 edges (+46 inverses), burrow-temporal 54->112 (+58; 4 supersede chains intact), trivyn-temporal 186->419 (+233; asserted edge:node 0.45->1.01, 42 chains intact). The new MOOSE core full-text-search (#42)/search_records (#41) also applies at query time after the re-serve. For incremental COMMIT catch-up (a graph N commits behind main) use temporal_bootstrap.py --resume: a per-store temporal-applied.log cursor re-enumerates the live trunk, skips already-applied SHAs, and captures only the new tip episodes (assumes append-only trunk; cursor must travel with the store). The snapshot skill bootstrap-existing-codebase has NO commit cursor — it re-surveys from scratch." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/613cb623-9ee8-4eaa-80db-c1e8e83b40f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/613cb623-9ee8-4eaa-80db-c1e8e83b40f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-22T20:08:17.664703Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/613cb623-9ee8-4eaa-80db-c1e8e83b40f3> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Modernize a pre-GROWL store by re-serving, not re-bootstrapping" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a2bf1670-239d-40d4-8f7c-f87b095c0c90> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a2bf1670-239d-40d4-8f7c-f87b095c0c90> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mine spec files for Requirements during bootstrap" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a2bf1670-239d-40d4-8f7c-f87b095c0c90> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a2bf1670-239d-40d4-8f7c-f87b095c0c90> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "When bootstrapping a codebase, files clearly identifiable as specifications — under a spec/ directory, or self-identifying as a spec/specification — are a dense, high-quality source to mine for Requirement records. Specs state intended behavior and constraints directly, so they map cleanly to typed Requirements that downstream ArchitecturalDecisions can be isMotivatedBy. WHY THIS MATTERS: the dogfood graph is Requirement-sparse (~13 Requirements for 39 decisions), which is exactly why most decisions could not be honestly linked to a motivating Requirement during the link-backfill (anti-confabulation forced skipping them). Mining specs up front mints the Requirement hubs that make isMotivatedBy edges — and structural-NLQ traversal from requirement → motivated decisions — possible. Bootstrapper guidance (user-provided); operationalize in skills/bootstrap-existing-codebase.md alongside the decision-cluster capture phase." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a2bf1670-239d-40d4-8f7c-f87b095c0c90> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a2bf1670-239d-40d4-8f7c-f87b095c0c90> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-22T15:02:22.252206Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a2bf1670-239d-40d4-8f7c-f87b095c0c90> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Mine spec files for Requirements during bootstrap" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a820e93a-131b-41fd-bb53-5bc4607ccb7b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a820e93a-131b-41fd-bb53-5bc4607ccb7b> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Generated artifact pages use shared UI shell components" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a820e93a-131b-41fd-bb53-5bc4607ccb7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex-mcp-client" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a820e93a-131b-41fd-bb53-5bc4607ccb7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Generated artifact pages should keep common list/detail/archive/refresh/warning/markdown-navigation behavior in a shared UI shell component, while each artifact page provides only artifact-specific configuration such as API calls, labels, warning summaries, row metadata, and record prefixes. This keeps ADR and Requirements pages behaviorally aligned and makes future generated artifact pages cheaper to add without copying page-state and layout code." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a820e93a-131b-41fd-bb53-5bc4607ccb7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a820e93a-131b-41fd-bb53-5bc4607ccb7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-26T04:18:00.516661Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/a820e93a-131b-41fd-bb53-5bc4607ccb7b> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Generated artifact pages use shared UI shell components" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Deterministic per-RFC bootstrap of the rust-lang/rfcs benchmark corpus" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Phase-3 public thesis corpus is provisioned and frozen. Source: fresh clone of rust-lang/rfcs pinned at SHA 7160a96b584ddd8b80128d90f0cf41b0eaa26a3e, under ~/code/moosedev_benches/rust-rfcs (BENCH_HOME; gitignored, outside the open repo). Method (bench/bootstrap_rust_rfcs.py): deterministic, no-LLM extraction — one merged RFC (text/NNNN-name.md) → one ArchitecturalDecision record; title = \"RFC N: feature\"; description = the RFC's OWN sections (## Summary + Motivation/Problems + Rationale and alternatives/Alternatives + Drawbacks), the why & why-not, captured verbatim, each section capped at 1800 chars. Writes go through ONE persistent MCP session to an explicit `moosedev --serve` backend on the per-corpus data dir (BENCH_HOME/rust-rfcs/.moosedev) with MOOSEDEV_NO_AUTOSPAWN=1 and the shared ontology dir (avoids the backend-lifecycle thrash of Lesson a7dec1f3). Result: 634 records written in 0.3s (record_important_decision is symbolic — no per-record LLM); validate_against_architecture → Conforms, 0 violations; B1 export (corpus/rust-rfcs.json) via sparql = 634 chunks; parity_check.py confirms chunks == graph records and every chunk body == the graph's stored hasDescription (PARITY OK). Capture policy honored: grading ground truth will be the RFC text in the working tree, never these records (no circularity). Limitation: record_important_decision can't yet write object properties, so RFC-to-RFC cross-references live in the description text (not yet typed relations) and supersede chains aren't asserted — see Requirement b2f8240c; multi-hop tasks rely on textual references for now, and H4 supersession will be exercised via explicit supersede_decision calls in task design. Trivyn corpus (private, strong-model synthesis) is the remaining Phase-3 item." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-18T17:12:46.642762Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/c6010de5-9bdd-4e46-90a6-a7f48c6819ce> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Deterministic per-RFC bootstrap of the rust-lang/rfcs benchmark corpus (634 records, content parity via sparql)" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d7b2801b-6cb4-46ad-88bd-2b5d92e9f373> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Pattern> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d7b2801b-6cb4-46ad-88bd-2b5d92e9f373> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "trivyn benchmark corpus bootstrapped via strong-model synthesis" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d7b2801b-6cb4-46ad-88bd-2b5d92e9f373> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/ce49a867-7ebc-41d5-879c-fa59eed3ae65> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d7b2801b-6cb4-46ad-88bd-2b5d92e9f373> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Pattern/d7b2801b-6cb4-46ad-88bd-2b5d92e9f373> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Phase-3b private thesis corpus is provisioned. Source: pinned clone of trivyn (origin Trivyn/trivyn, PRIVATE) at SHA 1e6e44dff78038d7e3cca6c6439e8f8cacda0d63, under ~/code/moosedev_benches/trivyn — clone, graph, B1 export, tasks, and run transcripts all stay in BENCH_HOME, never the open repo. Method (bench/bootstrap-existing-codebase skill): 6 read-only survey subagents in parallel, each over a subsystem cluster (architecture & MOOSE boundary; ingestion & extraction; ontologies/alignment/SHACL; graph/DB/SPARQL/AI; frontend & conventions; pitfalls & git history), each reading the spec/ files, docs-dev handbook chapters, CONVENTIONS, and git log and returning high-signal typed records (kind/title/description + evidence) under the capture-vs-skip bar. ~100 candidates consolidated/deduped to 89 (records.json), written via bench/bootstrap_trivyn.py through one persistent MCP session to the per-corpus backend (BENCH_HOME/trivyn/.moosedev, NO_AUTOSPAWN). Distribution: 32 ArchitecturalDecision, 20 Constraint, 16 Lesson, 11 Pattern, 9 AntiPattern, 1 Requirement — decision/constraint/anti-pattern dense, suited to constraint-adherence CODE tasks (the real value signal, unlike self-documenting moosedev-on-itself) and why/why-not multi-hop Q&A. validate_against_architecture → 0 violations; B1 export (trivyn.json in BENCH_HOME) = 89 chunks; parity_check → PARITY OK. Grading ground truth for trivyn tasks will be the trivyn docs/code itself, never these records (capture policy). Phase 3 (rust-rfcs + trivyn) now complete; see Pattern c6010de5 (rust-rfcs). Remaining gate before the headline runs: moose search_records (fair B2 retrieval)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
