<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/74423463-3982-4620-b8bd-f72e5987778e> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/74423463-3982-4620-b8bd-f72e5987778e> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Migrate existing A-box instances on breaking ontology change" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/74423463-3982-4620-b8bd-f72e5987778e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/74423463-3982-4620-b8bd-f72e5987778e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "The vector-store cache keeps only the T-box (ontology term embeddings) fresh; it does nothing for captured A-box instances. A cache hit therefore does not imply recorded data is still valid. A breaking ontology change (renamed/removed class, namespace shift) orphans existing instances, which store concrete class/property IRIs resolved at capture time. Need an explicit migration triggered on a detected ontology-version change (re-type via a mapping — never hardcode old namespaces). Additive ontology changes (new classes/properties, stable IRIs) need no A-box migration. The fingerprint cache is forward-compatible: an ontology change flips the fingerprint and forces a vector rebuild, which can be the same trigger point for the A-box migration. Tracked as P1 in tasks/todo.md (Ontology-regeneration orphans existing records)." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/74423463-3982-4620-b8bd-f72e5987778e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/74423463-3982-4620-b8bd-f72e5987778e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-06-17T23:14:05.727497Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/74423463-3982-4620-b8bd-f72e5987778e> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "Migrate existing A-box instances on breaking ontology change" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CodeEntity workbench exposes trusted source context" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/19df26dc-076b-4339-bee6-bfdc602c13ff> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/6baa075c-db0d-48e0-800a-0cae86603b2a> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/8d48edbd-7ee2-4a52-9eac-f2a09c858637> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#concerns> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/SystemComponent/accf4f9f-6309-4d3f-8705-26e551824eb0> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "claude-code" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "Claim: a CodeEntity's canonical workbench record page must be a source-aware destination, and an editor hover must be able to reach the Story for the exact entity under the cursor. Refines Requirement 9327d3b1 (cohesive evidence-backed Stories) at the code-entity end.\n\nToday a CodeEntity resolved through #/record/{uuid} renders with the same generic presentation as an ArchitecturalDecision: title, lifecycle metadata, and a relationship graph. That is comprehension debt at the point of maximum need — the reader arrived from a hover or a Story code anchor asking \"what is this thing\", and the page cannot show the code, its kind, its signature, or where it lives. Symmetrically, the LSP hover is already the highest-frequency knowledge surface but is a dead end: it lists records without offering the cohesive account of the entity it just described.\n\nWHAT IS REQUIRED. (1) The record detail read model carries optional CodeEntity metadata — substrate symbol, code name and kind, logical and defining paths, signature, current definition range, and whether source is available. (2) A bounded source read is available beside it: definition-plus-context and whole-indexed-file scopes, with 1-based UTF-8 byte coordinates. (3) The WebUI renders that as a line-numbered viewer above the relationship graph, with definition lines marked and an explicit explanation whenever source cannot be trusted. (4) \"Tell this Story\" on a CodeEntity launches the Story for that exact entity rather than redirecting to its containing component, and a canonical #/stories/entity/{uuid} deep link makes that destination refreshable and linkable. (5) The hover carries that link near the top, using the daemon's live published HTTP address and omitting it when the workbench is not serving.\n\nWHAT IS NOT REQUIRED. Source locations stay runtime substrate projections; nothing here becomes a new graph claim, a new ontology term, or a capture-pipeline change. Source viewing stays in the WebUI — no local IDE or file:// hand-off. The existing hover-silence rule is preserved: an entity with no direct records and no judgments still produces no hover, so the link never manufactures a reason to interrupt." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "accepted" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTimestamp> "2026-08-16T02:04:48.908744Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/7f838a91-3e33-44fd-a988-57a5bf6dfaee> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasTitle> "CodeEntity workbench exposes trusted source context" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/8b56c342-90f7-46b3-8667-ce76a2977883> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#Requirement> <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/8b56c342-90f7-46b3-8667-ce76a2977883> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Human-facing grounded Stories across project subjects" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/8b56c342-90f7-46b3-8667-ce76a2977883> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasAuthor> "codex" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/8b56c342-90f7-46b3-8667-ce76a2977883> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasDescription> "MOOSEDev must let humans recover a concise, evidence-backed explanation anchored to a current SystemComponent, InformationRecord, or CodeEntity, or to a bounded free-form topic retrieval. Every factual beat must expose current graph records and code anchors selected by deterministic subject-family planning; topic queries remain presentation metadata rather than project facts. Entity and topic routes must support generated, draft, and published forms. The default reboarding experience must use plain-language guidance, visibly distinguish LLM-assisted prose from intentional symbolic prose and safe fallback, and remain fully usable without an LLM. When the graph cannot support a beat or nontrivial comprehension check, Story must expose an explicit gap rather than invent content." <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
<https://moosedev.dev/kg/Requirement/8b56c342-90f7-46b3-8667-ce76a2977883> <https://trivyn.io/ontologies/software/architecture#hasLifecycleStatus> "superseded" <https://moosedev.dev/kg/project> .
